.SH About zclone {#about}
Zclone is a command-line program to manage files on cloud storage. It
is a feature-rich alternative to cloud vendors' web storage
interfaces. Over 70 cloud storage products
\[la]#providers\[ra] support
zclone including S3 object stores, business & consumer file storage
services, as well as standard transfer protocols.

.PP
Zclone has powerful cloud equivalents to the unix commands rsync, cp,
mv, mount, ls, ncdu, tree, rm, and cat. Zclone's familiar syntax
includes shell pipeline support, and \fB--dry-run\fR protection. It is
used at the command line, in scripts or via its API
\[la]/rc\[ra]\&.

.PP
Users call zclone \fI"The Swiss army knife of cloud storage"\fP, and
\fI"Technology indistinguishable from magic"\fP\&.

.PP
Zclone really looks after your data. It preserves timestamps and
verifies checksums at all times. Transfers over limited bandwidth;
intermittent connections, or subject to quota can be restarted, from
the last good file transferred. You can
check
\[la]//commands/zclone_check/\[ra] the integrity of your files. Where
possible, zclone employs server-side transfers to minimise local
bandwidth use and transfers from one provider to another without
using local disk.

.PP
Virtual backends wrap local and cloud file systems to apply
encryption
\[la]//crypt/\[ra],
compression
\[la]//compress/\[ra],
chunking
\[la]//chunker/\[ra],
hashing
\[la]//hasher/\[ra] and
joining
\[la]//union/\[ra]\&.

.PP
Zclone mounts
\[la]//commands/zclone_mount/\[ra] any local, cloud or
virtual filesystem as a disk on Windows,
macOS, linux and FreeBSD, and also serves these over
SFTP
\[la]//commands/zclone_serve_sftp/\[ra],
HTTP
\[la]//commands/zclone_serve_http/\[ra],
WebDAV
\[la]//commands/zclone_serve_webdav/\[ra],
FTP
\[la]//commands/zclone_serve_ftp/\[ra] and
DLNA
\[la]//commands/zclone_serve_dlna/\[ra]\&.

.PP
Zclone is mature, open-source software originally inspired by rsync
and written in Go
\[la]https://golang.org\[ra]\&. The friendly support
community is familiar with varied use cases. Official Ubuntu, Debian,
Fedora, Brew and Chocolatey repos. include zclone. For the latest
version downloading from zclone.org
\[la]//downloads/\[ra] is recommended.

.PP
Zclone is widely used on Linux, Windows and Mac. Third-party
developers create innovative backup, restore, GUI and business
process solutions using the zclone command line or API.

.PP
Zclone does the heavy lifting of communicating with cloud storage.

.SH What can zclone do for you? {#what}
Zclone helps you:
.IP \(bu 2
Backup (and encrypt) files to cloud storage
.IP \(bu 2
Restore (and decrypt) files from cloud storage
.IP \(bu 2
Mirror cloud data to other cloud services or locally
.IP \(bu 2
Migrate data to the cloud, or between cloud storage vendors
.IP \(bu 2
Mount multiple, encrypted, cached or diverse cloud storage as a disk
.IP \(bu 2
Analyse and account for data held on cloud storage using lsf
\[la]//commands/zclone_lsf/\[ra],
ljson
\[la]//commands/zclone_lsjson/\[ra], size
\[la]//commands/zclone_size/\[ra], ncdu
\[la]//commands/zclone_ncdu/\[ra]
.IP \(bu 2
Union
\[la]//union/\[ra] file systems together to present multiple local and/or cloud
file systems as one

