.SH Basic syntax
Zclone syncs a directory tree from one storage system to another.

.PP
Its syntax is like this

.EX
zclone subcommand [options] <parameters> <parameters...>
.EE

.PP
A \fBsubcommand\fR is an zclone operation required (e.g. \fBsync\fR,
\fBcopy\fR, \fBls\fR).

.PP
An \fBoption\fR is a single letter flag (e.g. \fB-v\fR) or a group of single
letter flags (e.g. \fB-Pv\fR) or a long flag (e.g. \fB--progress\fR). No
options are required. Options can come after the \fBsubcommand\fR or in
between parameters too or on the end, but only global options can be
used before the \fBsubcommand\fR\&. Anything after a \fB--\fR option will not be
interpreted as an option so if you need to add a parameter which
starts with a \fB-\fR then put a \fB--\fR on its own first, eg

.EX
zclone lsf -- -directory-starting-with-dash
.EE

.PP
A \fBparameter\fR is usually a file path or zclone remote
\[la]#syntax\-of\-remote\-paths\[ra],
eg \fB/path/to/file\fR or \fBremote:path/to/file\fR but it can be other things -
the \fBsubcommand\fR help will tell you what.

.PP
Source and destination paths are specified by the name you gave the
storage system in the config file then the sub path, e.g.
"drive:myfolder" to look at "myfolder" in Google drive.

.PP
You can define as many storage paths as you like in the config file.

.PP
Please use the 
\[la]#interactive\[ra] flag while
learning zclone to avoid accidental data loss.

.SH Subcommands
zclone uses a system of subcommands. For example

.EX
zclone ls remote:path # lists a remote
zclone copy /local/path remote:path # copies /local/path to the remote
zclone sync --interactive /local/path remote:path # syncs /local/path to the remote
.EE


.SH zclone config
Enter an interactive configuration session.

.SH Synopsis
Enter an interactive configuration session where you can setup new
remotes and manage existing ones. You may also set or remove a
password to protect your configuration.

.EX
zclone config [flags]
.EE

.SH Options
.EX
  -h, --help   help for config
.EE

.PP
See the global flags page
\[la]//flags/\[ra] for global options not listed here.

