.SH zclone purge
Remove the path and all of its contents.

.SH Synopsis
Remove the path and all of its contents.  Note that this does not obey
include/exclude filters - everything will be removed.  Use the
delete
\[la]//commands/zclone_delete/\[ra] command if you want to selectively
delete files. To delete empty directories only, use command
rmdir
\[la]//commands/zclone_rmdir/\[ra] or rmdirs
\[la]//commands/zclone_rmdirs/\[ra]\&.

.PP
The concurrency of this operation is controlled by the \fB--checkers\fR global flag.
However, some backends will implement this command directly, in which
case \fB--checkers\fR will be ignored.

.PP
\fBImportant\fP: Since this can cause data loss, test first with the
\fB--dry-run\fR or the \fB--interactive\fR/\fB-i\fR flag.

.EX
zclone purge remote:path [flags]
