.SH zclone about
Get quota information from the remote.

.SH Synopsis
Prints quota information about a remote to standard
output. The output is typically used, free, quota and trash contents.

.PP
E.g. Typical output from \fBzclone about remote:\fR is:

.EX
Total:   17 GiB
Used:    7.444 GiB
Free:    1.315 GiB
Trashed: 100.000 MiB
Other:   8.241 GiB
.EE

.PP
Where the fields are:
.IP \(bu 2
Total: Total size available.
.IP \(bu 2
Used: Total size used.
.IP \(bu 2
Free: Total space available to this user.
.IP \(bu 2
Trashed: Total space used by trash.
.IP \(bu 2
Other: Total amount in other storage (e.g. Gmail, Google Photos).
.IP \(bu 2
Objects: Total number of objects in the storage.

.PP
All sizes are in number of bytes.

.PP
Applying a \fB--full\fR flag to the command prints the bytes in full, e.g.

.EX
Total:   18253611008
Used:    7993453766
Free:    1411001220
Trashed: 104857602
Other:   8849156022
.EE

.PP
A \fB--json\fR flag generates conveniently machine-readable output, e.g.

.EX
{
  "total": 18253611008,
  "used": 7993453766,
  "trashed": 104857602,
  "other": 8849156022,
  "free": 1411001220
}
.EE

.PP
Not all backends print all fields. Information is not included if it is not
provided by a backend. Where the value is unlimited it is omitted.

.PP
Some backends does not support the \fBzclone about\fR command at all,
see complete list in documentation
\[la]///overview/#optional\-features\[ra]\&.

.EX
zclone about remote: [flags]
.EE

.SH Options
.EX
      --full   Full numbers instead of human-readable
  -h, --help   help for about
      --json   Format output as JSON
.EE

.PP
See the global flags page
\[la]//flags/\[ra] for global options not listed here.

.SH See Also
.IP \(bu 2
zclone
\[la]//commands/zclone/\[ra]	 - Show help for zclone commands, flags and backends.


.SH zclone archive
Perform an action on an archive.

.SH Synopsis
Perform an action on an archive. Requires the use of a
subcommand to specify the protocol, e.g.

.EX
zclone archive list remote:file.zip
.EE

.PP
Each subcommand has its own options which you can see in their help.

.PP
See zclone archive create
\[la]//commands/zclone_archive_create/\[ra] for the
archive formats supported.

.EX
zclone archive <action> [opts] <source> [<destination>] [flags]
.EE

.SH Options
.EX
  -h, --help   help for archive
.EE

.PP
See the global flags page
\[la]//flags/\[ra] for global options not listed here.

.SH See Also
.IP \(bu 2
zclone
\[la]//commands/zclone/\[ra]	 - Show help for zclone commands, flags and backends.
.IP \(bu 2
