.SH zclone config unset
Unset options in an existing remote.

.SH Synopsis
Remove one or more options from an existing remote. The options to
remove should be passed in as a list of key names.

.PP
For example, to remove the \fBclient_id\fR and \fBclient_secret\fR options from
a remote of name myremote you would do:

.EX
zclone config unset myremote client_id client_secret
.EE

.PP
This removes the keys from the config file entirely, which is different
from setting them to an empty string with \fBconfig update\fR\&. Removing a
key restores zclone's default behaviour for that option, whereas setting
it to an empty string overrides the default with an empty value.

.PP
You can't unset the \fBtype\fR of a remote - use \fBconfig delete\fR to remove
the whole remote instead.

.EX
zclone config unset name [key]+ [flags]
.EE

.SH Options
.EX
  -h, --help   help for unset
.EE

