.SH Limitations
\fBzclone about\fR is not supported by the 1Fichier backend. Backends without
this capability cannot determine free space for an zclone mount or
use policy \fBmfs\fR (most free space) as a member of an zclone union
remote.

.PP
See List of backends that do not support zclone about
\[la]///overview/#optional\-features\[ra]
and zclone about
\[la]///commands/zclone_about/\[ra]\&.


.SH Alias
The \fBalias\fR remote provides a new name for another remote.

.PP
Paths may be as deep as required or a local path,
e.g. \fBremote:directory/subdirectory\fR or \fB/directory/subdirectory\fR\&.

.PP
During the initial setup with \fBzclone config\fR you will specify the target
remote. The target remote can either be a local path or another remote.

.PP
Subfolders can be used in target remote. Assume an alias remote named \fBbackup\fR
with the target \fBmydrive:private/backup\fR\&. Invoking \fBzclone mkdir backup:desktop\fR
is exactly the same as invoking \fBzclone mkdir mydrive:private/backup/desktop\fR\&.

.PP
There will be no special handling of paths containing \fB\&..\fR segments.
Invoking \fBzclone mkdir backup:../desktop\fR is exactly the same as invoking
\fBzclone mkdir mydrive:private/backup/../desktop\fR\&.
The empty path is not allowed as a remote. To alias the current directory
use \fB\&.\fR instead.

.PP
The target remote can also be a connection string
\[la]//docs/#connection\-strings\[ra]\&.
This can be used to modify the config of a remote for different uses, e.g.
the alias  \fBmyDriveTrash\fR with the target remote \fBmyDrive,trashed_only:\fR
can be used to only show the trashed files in \fBmyDrive\fR\&.

