.SS --s3-use-already-exists
Set if zclone should report BucketAlreadyExists errors on bucket creation.

.PP
At some point during the evolution of the s3 protocol, AWS started
returning an \fBAlreadyOwnedByYou\fR error when attempting to create a
bucket that the user already owned, rather than a
\fBBucketAlreadyExists\fR error.

.PP
Unfortunately exactly what has been implemented by s3 clones is a
little inconsistent, some return \fBAlreadyOwnedByYou\fR, some return
\fBBucketAlreadyExists\fR and some return no error at all.

.PP
This is important to zclone because it ensures the bucket exists by
creating it on quite a lot of operations (unless
\fB--s3-no-check-bucket\fR is used).

.PP
If zclone knows the provider can return \fBAlreadyOwnedByYou\fR or returns
no error then it can report \fBBucketAlreadyExists\fR errors when the user
attempts to create a bucket not owned by them. Otherwise zclone
ignores the \fBBucketAlreadyExists\fR error which can lead to confusion.

.PP
This should be automatically set correctly for all providers zclone
knows about - please make a bug report if not.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      use_already_exists
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_S3_USE_ALREADY_EXISTS
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        Tristate
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     unset

.SS --s3-use-multipart-uploads
Set if zclone should use multipart uploads.

.PP
You can change this if you want to disable the use of multipart uploads.
This shouldn't be necessary in normal operation.

.PP
This should be automatically set correctly for all providers zclone
knows about - please make a bug report if not.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      use_multipart_uploads
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_S3_USE_MULTIPART_UPLOADS
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        Tristate
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     unset

.SS --s3-list-versions-oldest-first
Set if the backend returns object versions oldest first.

.PP
The S3 standard returns object versions newest first. Some backends
(e.g. Hitachi HCP) return them oldest first instead.

.PP
Set this quirk if --s3-version-at or --s3-versions produce incorrect
results with your backend.

.PP
This should be automatically set correctly for all providers zclone
knows about - please make a bug report if not.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      list_versions_oldest_first
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_S3_LIST_VERSIONS_OLDEST_FIRST
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        Tristate
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     unset

.SS --s3-use-x-id
Set if zclone should add x-id URL parameters.

.PP
You can change this if you want to disable the AWS SDK from
adding x-id URL parameters.

.PP
This shouldn't be necessary in normal operation.

.PP
This should be automatically set correctly for all providers zclone
knows about - please make a bug report if not.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      use_x_id
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_S3_USE_X_ID
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        Tristate
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     unset

.SS --s3-sign-accept-encoding
Set if zclone should include Accept-Encoding as part of the signature.

.PP
You can change this if you want to stop zclone including
Accept-Encoding as part of the signature.

.PP
This shouldn't be necessary in normal operation.

.PP
This should be automatically set correctly for all providers zclone
knows about - please make a bug report if not.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      sign_accept_encoding
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_S3_SIGN_ACCEPT_ENCODING
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        Tristate
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     unset

.SS --s3-directory-bucket
Set to use AWS Directory Buckets

.PP
If you are using an AWS Directory Bucket then set this flag.

.PP
This will ensure no \fBContent-Md5\fR headers are sent and ensure \fBETag\fR
headers are not interpreted as MD5 sums. \fBX-Amz-Meta-Md5chksum\fR will
be set on all objects whether single or multipart uploaded.

.PP
This also sets \fBno_check_bucket = true\fR\&.

.PP
Note that Directory Buckets do not support:
.IP \(bu 2
Versioning
.IP \(bu 2
\fBContent-Encoding: gzip\fR

.PP
Zclone limitations with Directory Buckets:
.IP \(bu 2
zclone does not support creating Directory Buckets with \fBzclone mkdir\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\&... or removing them with \fBzclone rmdir\fR yet
.IP \(bu 2
Directory Buckets do not appear when doing \fBzclone lsf\fR at the top level.
.IP \(bu 2
Zclone can't remove auto created directories yet. In theory this should
work with \fBdirectory_markers = true\fR but it doesn't.
.IP \(bu 2
Directories don't seem to appear in recursive (ListR) listings.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      directory_bucket
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_S3_DIRECTORY_BUCKET
.IP \(bu 2
Provider:    AWS
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        bool
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     false

