.SS BizflyCloud {#bizflycloud}
Bizfly Cloud Simple Storage
\[la]https://bizflycloud.vn/simple\-storage\[ra] is an
S3-compatible service with regions in Hanoi (HN) and Ho Chi Minh City (HCM).

.PP
Use the endpoint for your region:
.IP \(bu 2
HN: \fBhn.ss.bfcplatform.vn\fR
.IP \(bu 2
HCM: \fBhcm.ss.bfcplatform.vn\fR

.PP
A minimal configuration looks like this.

.EX
[bizfly]
type = s3
provider = BizflyCloud
env_auth = false
access_key_id = YOUR_ACCESS_KEY
secret_access_key = YOUR_SECRET_KEY
region = HN
endpoint = hn.ss.bfcplatform.vn
location_constraint =
acl =
server_side_encryption =
storage_class =
.EE

.PP
Switch \fBregion\fR and \fBendpoint\fR to \fBHCM\fR and \fBhcm.ss.bfcplatform.vn\fR for Ho Chi
Minh City.

.SS Ceph
Ceph
\[la]https://ceph.com/\[ra] is an open-source, unified, distributed
storage system designed for excellent performance, reliability and
scalability.  It has an S3 compatible object storage interface.

.PP
To use zclone with Ceph, configure as above but leave the region blank
and set the endpoint.  You should end up with something like this in
your config:

.EX
[ceph]
type = s3
provider = Ceph
env_auth = false
access_key_id = XXX
secret_access_key = YYY
region =
endpoint = https://ceph.endpoint.example.com
location_constraint =
acl =
server_side_encryption =
storage_class =
.EE

.PP
If you are using an older version of CEPH (e.g. 10.2.x Jewel) and a
version of zclone before v1.59 then you may need to supply the
parameter \fB--s3-upload-cutoff 0\fR or put this in the config file as
\fBupload_cutoff 0\fR to work around a bug which causes uploading of small
files to fail.

.PP
Note also that Ceph sometimes puts \fB/\fR in the passwords it gives
users.  If you read the secret access key using the command line tools
you will get a JSON blob with the \fB/\fR escaped as \fB\\/\fR\&.  Make sure you
only write \fB/\fR in the secret access key.

.PP
Eg the dump from Ceph looks something like this (irrelevant keys
removed).

.EX
{
    "user_id": "xxx",
    "display_name": "xxxx",
    "keys": [
        {
            "user": "xxx",
            "access_key": "xxxxxx",
            "secret_key": "xxxxxx\\/xxxx"
        }
    ],
}
.EE

.PP
Because this is a json dump, it is encoding the \fB/\fR as \fB\\/\fR, so if you
use the secret key as \fBxxxxxx/xxxx\fR  it will work fine.

