.SS Modification times and hashes
Box allows modification times to be set on objects accurate to 1
second.  These will be used to detect whether objects need syncing or
not.

.PP
Box supports SHA1 type hashes, so you can use the \fB--checksum\fR
flag.

.SS Restricted filename characters
In addition to the default restricted characters set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]
the following characters are also replaced:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
	0x5C	＼
.TE

.PP
File names can also not end with the following characters.
These only get replaced if they are the last character in the name:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
SP	0x20	␠
.TE

.PP
Invalid UTF-8 bytes will also be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra],
as they can't be used in JSON strings.

.SS Transfers
For files above 50 MiB zclone will use a chunked transfer.  Zclone will
upload up to \fB--transfers\fR chunks at the same time (shared among all
the multipart uploads).  Chunks are buffered in memory and are
normally 8 MiB so increasing \fB--transfers\fR will increase memory use.

.SS Deleting files
Depending on the enterprise settings for your user, the item will
either be actually deleted from Box or moved to the trash.

.PP
Emptying the trash is supported via the zclone however cleanup command
however this deletes every trashed file and folder individually so it
may take a very long time.
Emptying the trash via the  WebUI does not have this limitation
so it is advised to empty the trash via the WebUI.

.SS Root folder ID
You can set the \fBroot_folder_id\fR for zclone.  This is the directory
(identified by its \fBFolder ID\fR) that zclone considers to be the root
of your Box drive.

.PP
Normally you will leave this blank and zclone will determine the
correct root to use itself.

.PP
However you can set this to restrict zclone to a specific folder
hierarchy.

.PP
In order to do this you will have to find the \fBFolder ID\fR of the
directory you wish zclone to display.  This will be the last segment
of the URL when you open the relevant folder in the Box web
interface.

.PP
So if the folder you want zclone to use has a URL which looks like
\fBhttps://app.box.com/folder/11xxxxxxxxx8\fR
in the browser, then you use \fB11xxxxxxxxx8\fR as
the \fBroot_folder_id\fR in the config.

.PP
 

