.SH Limitations
Note that Box is case insensitive so you can't have a file called
"Hello.doc" and one called "hello.doc".

.PP
Box file names can't have the \fB\\\fR character in.  zclone maps this to
and from an identical looking unicode equivalent \fB＼\fR (U+FF3C Fullwidth
Reverse Solidus).

.PP
Box only supports filenames up to 255 characters in length.

.PP
Box has API rate limits
\[la]https://developer.box.com/guides/api\-calls/permissions\-and\-errors/rate\-limits/\[ra]
that sometimes reduce the speed of zclone.

.PP
\fBzclone about\fR is not supported by the Box backend. Backends without
this capability cannot determine free space for an zclone mount or
use policy \fBmfs\fR (most free space) as a member of an zclone union
remote.

.PP
See List of backends that do not support zclone about
\[la]///overview/#optional\-features\[ra]
and zclone about
\[la]///commands/zclone_about/\[ra]\&.

.SH Get your own Box App ID
Here is how to create your own Box App ID for zclone:
.IP "  1." 5
Go to the Box Developer Console
\[la]https://app.box.com/developers/console\[ra]
and login, then click \fBMy Apps\fR on the sidebar. Click \fBCreate New App\fR
and select \fBCustom App\fR\&.
.IP "  2." 5
In the first screen on the box that pops up, you can pretty much enter
whatever you want. The \fBApp Name\fR can be whatever. For \fBPurpose\fR choose
automation to avoid having to fill out anything else. Click \fBNext\fR\&.
.IP "  3." 5
In the second screen of the creation screen, select
\fBUser Authentication (OAuth 2.0)\fR\&. Then click \fBCreate App\fR\&.
.IP "  4." 5
You should now be on the \fBConfiguration\fR tab of your new app. If not,
click on it at the top of the webpage. Copy down \fBClient ID\fR
and \fBClient Secret\fR, you'll need those for zclone.
.IP "  5." 5
Under "OAuth 2.0 Redirect URI", add \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:53682/\fR
.IP "  6." 5
For \fBApplication Scopes\fR, select \fBRead all files and folders stored in Box\fR
and \fBWrite all files and folders stored in box\fR (assuming you want to do both).
Leave others unchecked. Click \fBSave Changes\fR at the top right.


.SH Cache
The \fBcache\fR remote wraps another existing remote and stores file structure
and its data for long running tasks like \fBzclone mount\fR\&.

.PP
It is \fBdeprecated\fP so not recommended for use with new installations
and may be removed at some point.

.SH Status
The cache backend code is working but it currently doesn't
have a maintainer so there are outstanding bugs
\[la]/\[ra] which aren't getting fixed.

.PP
The cache backend is due to be phased out in favour of the VFS caching
layer eventually which is more tightly integrated into zclone.

.PP
Until this happens we recommend only using the cache backend if you
find you can't work without it. There are many docs online describing
the use of the cache backend to minimize API hits and by-and-large
these are out of date and the cache backend isn't needed in those
scenarios any more.

.SH Configuration
To get started you just need to have an existing remote which can be configured
with \fBcache\fR\&.

.PP
Here is an example of how to make a remote called \fBtest-cache\fR\&.  First run:

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:

.EX
