.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_DROPBOX_DESCRIPTION
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        string
.IP \(bu 2
Required:    false

.SH Limitations
Note that Dropbox is case insensitive so you can't have a file called
"Hello.doc" and one called "hello.doc".

.PP
There are some file names such as \fBthumbs.db\fR which Dropbox can't
store.  There is a full list of them in the "Ignored Files" section
of this document
\[la]https://www.dropbox.com/en/help/145\[ra]\&.  Zclone will
issue an error message \fBFile name disallowed - not uploading\fR if it
attempts to upload one of those file names, but the sync won't fail.

.PP
Some errors may occur if you try to sync copyright-protected files
because Dropbox has its own copyright detector
\[la]https://techcrunch.com/2014/03/30/how\-dropbox\-knows\-when\-youre\-sharing\-copyrighted\-stuff\-without\-actually\-looking\-at\-your\-stuff/\[ra]
that prevents this sort of file being downloaded. This will return the error
\fBERROR : /path/to/your/file: Failed to copy: failed to open source object: path/restricted_content/.\fR

.PP
If you have more than 10,000 files in a directory then \fBzclone purge
dropbox:dir\fR will return the error \fBFailed to purge: There are too
many files involved in this operation\fR\&.  As a work-around do an
\fBzclone delete dropbox:dir\fR followed by an \fBzclone rmdir dropbox:dir\fR\&.

.PP
When using \fBzclone link\fR you'll need to set \fB--expire\fR if using a
non-personal account otherwise the visibility may not be correct.
(Note that \fB--expire\fR isn't supported on personal accounts). See the
forum discussion
\[la]/\[ra]
and the
dropbox SDK issue
\[la]https://github.com/dropbox/dropbox\-sdk\-go\-unofficial/issues/75\[ra]\&.

.PP
Modification times for Dropbox Paper documents are not exact, and
may  not change for some period after the document is edited.
To make sure you get recent changes in a sync, either wait an hour
or so, or use \fB--ignore-times\fR to force a full sync.

.SH Get your own Dropbox App ID
When you use zclone with Dropbox in its default configuration you are using
zclone's App ID. This is shared between all the zclone users.

.PP
Here is how to create your own Dropbox App ID for zclone:
.IP "  1." 5
Log into the Dropbox App console
\[la]https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps/create\[ra]
with your Dropbox Account (It need not to be the same account as the Dropbox you
want to access)
.IP "  2." 5
Choose an API => Usually this should be \fBDropbox API\fR
.IP "  3." 5
Choose the type of access you want to use => \fBFull Dropbox\fR or \fBApp Folder\fR\&.
If you want to use Team Folders, \fBFull Dropbox\fR is required
(see here
\[la]https://www.dropboxforum.com/t5/Dropbox\-API\-Support\-Feedback/How\-to\-create\-team\-folder\-inside\-my\-app\-s\-folder/m\-p/601005/highlight/true#M27911\[ra]).
.IP "  4." 5
Name your App. The app name is global, so you can't use \fBzclone\fR for example
.IP "  5." 5
Click the button \fBCreate App\fR
.IP "  6." 5
Switch to the \fBPermissions\fR tab. Enable at least the following permissions:
\fBaccount_info.read\fR, \fBfiles.metadata.write\fR, \fBfiles.content.write\fR, \fBfiles.content.read\fR,
\fBsharing.write\fR\&. The \fBfiles.metadata.read\fR and \fBsharing.read\fR checkboxes will be
marked too. Click \fBSubmit\fR
.IP "  7." 5
Switch to the \fBSettings\fR tab. Fill \fBOAuth2 - Redirect URIs\fR as \fBhttp://localhost:53682/\fR
and click on \fBAdd\fR
.IP "  8." 5
Find the \fBApp key\fR and \fBApp secret\fR values on the \fBSettings\fR tab. Use these
values in zclone config to add a new remote or edit an existing remote.
The \fBApp key\fR setting corresponds to \fBclient_id\fR in zclone config, the
\fBApp secret\fR corresponds to \fBclient_secret\fR


.SH Enterprise File Fabric
This backend supports Storage Made Easy's Enterprise File
Fabric™
\[la]https://storagemadeeasy.com/about/\[ra] which provides a software
solution to integrate and unify File and Object Storage accessible
through a global file system.

.SH Configuration
The initial setup for the Enterprise File Fabric backend involves
getting a token from the Enterprise File Fabric which you need to
do in your browser.  \fBzclone config\fR walks you through it.

.PP
Here is an example of how to make a remote called \fBremote\fR\&.  First run:

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:

.EX
No remotes found, make a new one?
n) New remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config
n/s/q> n
name> remote
Type of storage to configure.
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value
[snip]
XX / Enterprise File Fabric
   \\ "filefabric"
[snip]
Storage> filefabric
** See help for filefabric backend at: //filefabric/ **

URL of the Enterprise File Fabric to connect to
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
