.PP
Once configured you can then use \fBzclone\fR like this (replace \fBremote\fR with the
name you gave your remote):

.PP
List directories in top level of your Enterprise File Fabric

.EX
zclone lsd remote:
.EE

.PP
List all the files in your Enterprise File Fabric

.EX
zclone ls remote:
.EE

.PP
To copy a local directory to an Enterprise File Fabric directory called backup

.EX
zclone copy /home/source remote:backup
.EE

.SS Modification times and hashes
The Enterprise File Fabric allows modification times to be set on
files accurate to 1 second.  These will be used to detect whether
objects need syncing or not.

.PP
The Enterprise File Fabric does not support any data hashes at this time.

.SS Restricted filename characters
The default restricted characters set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]
will be replaced.

.PP
Invalid UTF-8 bytes will also be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra],
as they can't be used in JSON strings.

.SS Empty files
Empty files aren't supported by the Enterprise File Fabric. Zclone will therefore
upload an empty file as a single space with a mime type of
\fBapplication/vnd.zclone.empty.file\fR and files with that mime type are
treated as empty.

.SS Root folder ID
You can set the \fBroot_folder_id\fR for zclone.  This is the directory
(identified by its \fBFolder ID\fR) that zclone considers to be the root
of your Enterprise File Fabric.

.PP
Normally you will leave this blank and zclone will determine the
correct root to use itself.

.PP
However you can set this to restrict zclone to a specific folder
hierarchy.

.PP
In order to do this you will have to find the \fBFolder ID\fR of the
directory you wish zclone to display.  These aren't displayed in the
web interface, but you can use \fBzclone lsf\fR to find them, for example

.EX
$ zclone lsf --dirs-only -Fip --csv filefabric:
120673758,Burnt PDFs/
120673759,My Quick Uploads/
120673755,My Syncs/
120673756,My backups/
120673757,My contacts/
120673761,S3 Storage/
.EE

.PP
The ID for "S3 Storage" would be \fB120673761\fR\&.

.PP
 

