.SH Limitations
FTP servers acting as zclone remotes must support \fBpassive\fR mode.
The mode cannot be configured as \fBpassive\fR is the only supported one.
Zclone's FTP implementation is not compatible with \fBactive\fR mode
as the library it uses doesn't support it
\[la]https://github.com/jlaffaye/ftp/issues/29\[ra]\&.
This will likely never be supported due to security concerns.

.PP
Zclone's FTP backend does not support any checksums but can compare
file sizes.

.PP
\fBzclone about\fR is not supported by the FTP backend. Backends without
this capability cannot determine free space for an zclone mount or
use policy \fBmfs\fR (most free space) as a member of an zclone union
remote.

.PP
See List of backends that do not support zclone about
\[la]///overview/#optional\-features\[ra]
and zclone about
\[la]///commands/zclone_about/\[ra]\&.

.PP
The implementation of : \fB--dump headers\fR,
\fB--dump bodies\fR, \fB--dump auth\fR for debugging isn't the same as
for zclone HTTP based backends - it has less fine grained control.

.PP
\fB--timeout\fR isn't supported (but \fB--contimeout\fR is).

.PP
\fB--bind\fR isn't supported.

.PP
Zclone's FTP backend could support server-side move but does not
at present.

.PP
The \fBftp_proxy\fR environment variable is not currently supported.

.SS Modification times
File modification time (timestamps) is supported to 1 second resolution
for major FTP servers: ProFTPd, PureFTPd, VsFTPd, and FileZilla FTP server.
The \fBVsFTPd\fR server has non-standard implementation of time related protocol
commands and needs a special configuration setting: \fBwriting_mdtm = true\fR\&.

.PP
Support for precise file time with other FTP servers varies depending on what
protocol extensions they advertise. If all the \fBMLSD\fR, \fBMDTM\fR and \fBMFTM\fR
extensions are present, zclone will use them together to provide precise time.
Otherwise the times you see on the FTP server through zclone are those of the
last file upload.

.PP
You can use the following command to check whether zclone can use precise time
with your FTP server: \fBzclone backend features your_ftp_remote:\fR (the trailing
colon is important). Look for the number in the line tagged by \fBPrecision\fR
designating the remote time precision expressed as nanoseconds. A value of
\fB1000000000\fR means that file time precision of 1 second is available.
A value of \fB3153600000000000000\fR (or another large number) means "unsupported".


.SH Gofile
Gofile
\[la]https://gofile.io\[ra] is a content storage and distribution
platform. Its aim is to provide as much service as possible for free
or at a very low price.

.PP
The initial setup for Gofile involves logging in to the web interface
and going to the "My Profile" section. Copy the "Account API token"
for use in the config file.

.PP
Note that if you wish to connect zclone to Gofile you will need a
premium account.

.SH Configuration
Here is an example of how to make a remote called \fBremote\fR\&.  First run:

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:

.EX
No remotes found, make a new one?
n) New remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config
n/s/q> n

Enter name for new remote.
name> remote

Option Storage.
Type of storage to configure.
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value.
XX / Gofile
   \\ (gofile)
Storage> gofile

Option access_token.
API Access token
You can get this from the web control panel.
Enter a value. Press Enter to leave empty.
access_token> YOURACCESSTOKEN

Edit advanced config?
y) Yes
n) No (default)
y/n> n

Configuration complete.
Options:
- type: gofile
- access_token: YOURACCESSTOKEN
Keep this "remote" remote?
y) Yes this is OK (default)
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote
y/e/d> y
.EE

.PP
Once configured you can then use \fBzclone\fR like this (replace \fBremote\fR with the
name you gave your remote):

.PP
List directories and files in the top level of your Gofile

.EX
zclone lsf remote:
.EE

.PP
To copy a local directory to an Gofile directory called backup

.EX
zclone copy /home/source remote:backup
.EE

.SS Modification times and hashes
Gofile supports modification times with a resolution of 1 second.

.PP
Gofile supports MD5 hashes, so you can use the \fB--checksum\fR flag.

.SS Restricted filename characters
In addition to the default restricted characters set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]
the following characters are also replaced:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
!	0x21	！
"	0x22	＂
*	0x2A	＊
:	0x3A	：
<	0x3C	＜
>	0x3E	＞
?	0x3F	？
	0x5C	＼
|	0x7C	｜
.TE

.PP
File names can also not start or end with the following characters.
These only get replaced if they are the first or last character in the
name:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
\&.	0x2E	．
.TE

.PP
Invalid UTF-8 bytes will also be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra],
as they can't be used in JSON strings.

.SS Public Links
Gofile supports \fBzclone link\fR to make public links to files or
directories. If you specify a directory it will download as a \fBzip\fR
file. You can use the \fB--expire\fR flag to specify the time the link
should be valid. Note that \fBzclone link --unlink\fR removes all the
public links for a file.

.SS Root folder ID
You can set the \fBroot_folder_id\fR for zclone.  This is the directory
(identified by its \fBFolder ID\fR) that zclone considers to be the root
of your Gofile drive.

.PP
Normally you will leave this blank and zclone will determine the
correct root to use itself and fill in the value in the config file.

.PP
However you can set this to restrict zclone to a specific folder
hierarchy.

.PP
In order to do this you will have to find the \fBFolder ID\fR of the
directory you wish zclone to display.

.PP
You can do this with zclone

.EX
$ zclone lsf -Fip --dirs-only remote:
d6341f53-ee65-4f29-9f59-d11e8070b2a0;Files/
f4f5c9b8-6ece-478b-b03e-4538edfe5a1c;Photos/
d50e356c-29ca-4b27-a3a7-494d91026e04;Videos/
.EE

.PP
The ID to use is the part before the \fB;\fR so you could set

.EX
root_folder_id = d6341f53-ee65-4f29-9f59-d11e8070b2a0
.EE

.PP
To restrict zclone to the \fBFiles\fR directory.

.PP
 

