Leave blank to use the provider defaults.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      token_url
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_GCS_TOKEN_URL
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        string
.IP \(bu 2
Required:    false

.SS --gcs-client-credentials
Use client credentials OAuth flow.

.PP
This will use the OAUTH2 client Credentials Flow as described in RFC 6749.

.PP
Note that this option is NOT supported by all backends.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      client_credentials
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_GCS_CLIENT_CREDENTIALS
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        bool
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     false

.SS --gcs-access-token
Short-lived access token.

.PP
Leave blank normally.
Needed only if you want use short-lived access token instead of interactive login.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      access_token
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_GCS_ACCESS_TOKEN
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        string
.IP \(bu 2
Required:    false

.SS --gcs-directory-markers
Upload an empty object with a trailing slash when a new directory is created

.PP
Empty folders are unsupported for bucket based remotes, this option creates an empty
object ending with "/", to persist the folder.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      directory_markers
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_GCS_DIRECTORY_MARKERS
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        bool
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     false

.SS --gcs-no-check-bucket
If set, don't attempt to check the bucket exists or create it.

.PP
This can be useful when trying to minimise the number of transactions
zclone does if you know the bucket exists already.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      no_check_bucket
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_GCS_NO_CHECK_BUCKET
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        bool
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     false

.SS --gcs-decompress
If set this will decompress gzip encoded objects.

.PP
It is possible to upload objects to GCS with "Content-Encoding: gzip"
set. Normally zclone will download these files as compressed objects.

.PP
If this flag is set then zclone will decompress these files with
"Content-Encoding: gzip" as they are received. This means that zclone
can't check the size and hash but the file contents will be decompressed.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      decompress
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_GCS_DECOMPRESS
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        bool
.IP \(bu 2
Default:     false

.SS --gcs-endpoint
Custom endpoint for the storage API. Leave blank to use the provider default.

.PP
When using a custom endpoint that includes a subpath (e.g. example.org/custom/endpoint),
the subpath will be ignored during upload operations due to a limitation in the
underlying Google API Go client library.
Download and listing operations will work correctly with the full endpoint path.
If you require subpath support for uploads, avoid using subpaths in your custom
endpoint configuration.

.PP
Properties:
.IP \(bu 2
Config:      endpoint
.IP \(bu 2
Env Var:     ZCLONE_GCS_ENDPOINT
.IP \(bu 2
Type:        string
.IP \(bu 2
Required:    false
.IP \(bu 2
Examples:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
"storage.example.org"
.IP \(bu 2
Specify a custom endpoint
.IP \(bu 2
"storage.example.org:4443"
.IP \(bu 2
Specifying a custom endpoint with port
.IP \(bu 2
"storage.example.org:4443/gcs/api"
.IP \(bu 2
Specifying a subpath, see the note, uploads won't use the custom path!
.RE

