.EE

.SS stickyimport
Perform fast import of a SUM file.

.EX
zclone backend stickyimport remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE

.PP
Fill hash cache from a SUM file without verifying file fingerprints.

.PP
Usage example:

.EX
zclone backend stickyimport hasher:subdir md5 remote:path/to/sum.md5
.EE

.SH Implementation details (advanced)
This section explains how various zclone operations work on a hasher remote.

.PP
\fBDisclaimer. This section describes current implementation which can
change in future zclone versions!.\fP

.SS Hashsum command
The \fBzclone hashsum\fR (or \fBmd5sum\fR or \fBsha1sum\fR) command will:
.IP "  1." 5
if requested hash is supported by lower level, just pass it.
.IP "  2." 5
if object size is below \fBauto_size\fR then download object and calculate
\fIrequested\fP hashes on the fly.
.IP "  3." 5
if unsupported and the size is big enough, build object \fBfingerprint\fR
(including size, modtime if supported, first-found \fIother\fP hash if any).
.IP "  4." 5
if the strict match is found in cache for the requested remote, return
the stored hash.
.IP "  5." 5
if remote found but fingerprint mismatched, then purge the entry and
proceed to step 6.
.IP "  6." 5
if remote not found or had no requested hash type or after step 5:
download object, calculate all \fIsupported\fP hashes on the fly and store
in cache; return requested hash.

.SS Other operations
.IP \(bu 2
any time a hash is requested, follow the logic from 1-4 from \fBhashsum\fR above
.IP \(bu 2
whenever a file is uploaded or downloaded \fBin full\fP, capture the stream
to calculate all supported hashes on the fly and update database
.IP \(bu 2
server-side \fBmove\fR  will update keys of existing cache entries
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdeletefile\fR will remove a single cache entry
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpurge\fR will remove all cache entries under the purged path

.PP
Note that setting \fBmax_age = 0\fR will disable checksum caching completely.

.PP
If you set \fBmax_age = off\fR, checksums in cache will never age, unless you
fully rewrite or delete the file.

.SS Cache storage
Cached checksums are stored as \fBbolt\fR database files under zclone cache
directory, usually \fB~/.cache/zclone/kv/\fR\&. Databases are maintained
one per \fIbase\fP backend, named like \fBBaseRemote~hasher.bolt\fR\&.
Checksums for multiple \fBalias\fR-es into a single base backend
will be stored in the single database. All local paths are treated as
aliases into the \fBlocal\fR backend (unless encrypted or chunked) and stored
in \fB~/.cache/zclone/kv/local~hasher.bolt\fR\&.
Databases can be shared between multiple zclone processes.


.SH Huawei Drive
Paths are specified as \fBhuaweidrive:path\fR

.PP
Huawei Drive paths may be as deep as required, e.g. \fBhuaweidrive:directory/subdirectory\fR\&.

.SH Configuration
The initial setup for Huawei Drive involves getting a token from Huawei Drive
which you need to do in your browser. \fBzclone config\fR walks you
through it.

.PP
Here is an example of how to make a remote called \fBremote\fR\&. First run:

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:

.EX
No remotes found, make a new one?
n) New remote
r) Rename remote
c) Copy remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config
n/r/c/s/q> n
name> remote
Type of storage to configure.
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value
[snip]
XX / Huawei Drive
   \\ "huaweidrive"
[snip]
Storage> huaweidrive
OAuth Client Id - leave blank to use zclone's default.
client_id> 
OAuth Client Secret - leave blank to use zclone's default.
client_secret>
Remote config
Use web browser to automatically authenticate zclone with remote?
 * Say Y if the machine running zclone has a web browser you can use
 * Say N if running zclone on a (remote) machine without web browser access
If not sure try Y. If Y failed, try N.
y) Yes
n) No
y/n> y
If your browser doesn't open automatically go to the following link: http://127.0.0.1:53682/auth
Log in and authorize zclone for access
Waiting for code...
Got code
Configuration complete.
Options:
- type: huaweidrive
- client_id: 
- client_secret: 
- token: {"access_token":"XXX","token_type":"Bearer","refresh_token":"XXX","expiry":"2024-03-16T13:57:58.955387075Z"}
Keep this "remote" remote?
y) Yes this is OK
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote
y/e/d> y
.EE

.PP
See the remote setup docs
\[la]//remote_setup/\[ra] for how to set it up on a
machine without an internet-connected web browser available.

.PP
Note that zclone runs a webserver on your local machine to collect the
token as returned from Huawei if using web browser to automatically
authenticate. This only runs from the moment it opens your browser to the moment you get back
the verification code. This is on \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:53682/\fR and it
may require you to unblock it temporarily if you are running a host
firewall, or use manual mode.

.PP
You can then use it like this,

.PP
List directories in top level of your drive

.EX
zclone lsd remote:
.EE

.PP
List all the files in your drive

.EX
zclone ls remote:
.EE

.PP
To copy a local directory to a drive directory called backup

.EX
zclone copy /home/source remote:backup
.EE

.SS Getting your own Client ID and Secret
When you use zclone with Huawei Drive in its default configuration you
are using zclone's client_id. This is shared between all the zclone
users. There is a global rate limit on the number of queries per
second that each client_id can do set by Huawei.

.PP
It is strongly recommended to use your own client ID as the default zclone ID is heavily used. If you have multiple services running, it is recommended to use a separate client ID for each service to avoid rate limiting issues.

.PP
Here is how to create your own Huawei Drive client ID for zclone:

.PP
Follow the detailed guides for complete setup instructions:
.IP \(bu 2
Huawei HMS Core Web App Preparations
\[la]https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/HMSCore\-Guides/web\-preparations\-0000001050050891\[ra]
.IP \(bu 2
Huawei HMS Core Server Preparations
\[la]https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/HMSCore\-Guides/server\-preparations\-0000001050185577#section194911701377\[ra]

.PP
Zclone uses the web application access method to connect to Huawei Drive. Before starting, you need to implement quick login authorization through Huawei Account Open Service. With user authorization credentials, zclone can call Huawei Cloud Drive Service APIs.

.SS Create Server Application
Before accessing Drive service, developers need to create a server application first. For details, please refer to the WEB Application Access Development Preparation section in the "Huawei Account Service Development Guide".

.SS Enable Drive Application Switch
.IP "  1." 5
Log in to the AppGallery Connect website and click "My Projects".
.IP "  2." 5
Find your project in the project list, select the application that needs to access Drive in the project, and click "API Management".
.IP "  3." 5
In the "API Management" area of the "Project Settings" page, click the switch on the right side of Drive Kit to ensure the switch is in the open state.

.SS Sign Huawei Cloud Drive Privacy Notice and User Agreement
Guide users to visit 
\[la]https://cloud.huawei.com/\[ra]\&. First-time users need to sign the agreement before they can use Huawei Cloud Drive Service.

.SS Application Access to Obtain Authentication Credential Access Token
Applications accessing Drive should use authentication credential Access Token. For specific acquisition methods, please refer to the WEB Application Access Development Guide section in the "Huawei Account Service Development Guide".

.PP
Key steps summary:
.IP "  1." 5
Log into the Huawei Developer Console
\[la]https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/console\[ra] with your Huawei account.
.IP "  2." 5
Create a new project or select an existing project.
.IP "  3." 5
Go to "Manage APIs" and enable the "Drive Kit" API.
.IP "  4." 5
Click on "Credentials" in the left side panel.
.IP "  5." 5
Click "Create Credentials" and choose "OAuth client ID".
.IP "  6." 5
Choose "Web application" as the application type.
.IP "  7." 5
Add \fBhttp://localhost:53682/\fR to the "Authorized redirect URIs".
.IP "  8." 5
Click "Create" and note down the Client ID and Client Secret.
.IP "  9." 5
Provide the noted client ID and client secret to zclone during configuration.

.SS Scopes
Zclone uses the following OAuth2 scopes when accessing Huawei Drive:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhttps://www.huawei.com/auth/drive\fR - Full access to Huawei Drive files (excluding application data folder)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhttps://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.file\fR - Access to files created by the application
.IP \(bu 2
\fBopenid\fR - OpenID Connect authentication
.IP \(bu 2
\fBprofile\fR - Access to basic profile information

.PP
The \fBdrive.file\fR scope is included in the default set used by zclone.

.PP
Alternative scopes available (not used by zclone by default):
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhttps://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.appdata\fR - Access to application data folder
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhttps://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.readonly\fR - Read-only access to file metadata and content
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhttps://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.metadata\fR - Read/write access to file metadata only
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhttps://www.huawei.com/auth/drive.metadata.readonly\fR - Read-only access to file metadata only

.PP
The default scopes provide read/write access to all files in your Huawei Drive.

.SS Modification times and hashes
Huawei Drive does not support setting modification times. The API
always uses server-side timestamps, so file modification times from
the source are not preserved during upload. Modification times are
available as read-only metadata (\fBmtime\fR, \fBbtime\fR).

.PP
Hash algorithm SHA256 is supported for file integrity verification.

.SS Restricted filename characters
Huawei Drive has strict restrictions on file and directory names:
.IP \(bu 2
Cannot contain: \fB< > | : " * ? / \\\fR or emoji characters
.IP \(bu 2
Cannot be exactly \fB\&. ..\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum length: 250 bytes
.IP \(bu 2
Single quotes must be escaped with \fB\\'\fR in API calls

.PP
These restrictions are handled by zclone's encoding:
.IP \(bu 2
Backslashes \fB\\\fR are encoded
.IP \(bu 2
Invalid UTF-8 sequences are encoded
.br

.IP \(bu 2
Right-side spaces are encoded

.PP
Invalid characters will be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra] according to the encoding settings.

.SS Resumable uploads
Huawei Drive supports resumable uploads for files larger than the upload cutoff (default 20MB).
Files are uploaded in chunks which allows for recovery from network interruptions.

.SS File size limits
The maximum file size for Huawei Drive is 50 GiB.

.SS Quota information
To view your current quota you can use the \fBzclone about remote:\fR
command which will display your usage and quota information.

.PP
 

