.SH Limitations
Huawei Drive has some rate limiting which may cause zclone to slow down transfers to avoid hitting the limits.

.SS File name restrictions
.IP \(bu 2
File names cannot contain: \fB< > | : " * ? / \\\fR
.IP \(bu 2
File names cannot be exactly \fB\&. ..\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum file name length is 250 bytes
.IP \(bu 2
Some unicode characters including emojis are not supported

.SS API rate limits
Huawei Drive imposes API rate limits. Zclone automatically handles these by backing off when limits are hit.

.SS OAuth2 token expiry
.IP \(bu 2
Access tokens expire after 1 hour
.IP \(bu 2
Refresh tokens expire after 180 days
.br

.IP \(bu 2
Zclone will automatically refresh tokens as needed

.SS File size limits
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum file size is 50 GiB
.IP \(bu 2
Files larger than this cannot be uploaded

.SS Upload behavior
.IP \(bu 2
Files smaller than \fBupload_cutoff\fR (default 20MB) are uploaded in a single request using content or multipart method
.IP \(bu 2
Larger files are uploaded using resumable uploads with configurable chunk size
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum single chunk size for resumable uploads is 64MB
.IP \(bu 2
Resumable uploads support automatic retry on network errors
.IP \(bu 2
SHA256 hash verification is supported for uploaded files

.SS Server-side operations
.IP \(bu 2
Server-side copy: Files can be copied within Huawei Drive without downloading and re-uploading
.IP \(bu 2
Server-side move: Files and directories can be moved/renamed on the server side
.IP \(bu 2
Directory move: Entire directories can be moved with a single API call

.SS Directory operations
.IP \(bu 2
Huawei Drive supports creating empty directories
.IP \(bu 2
Recursive listing is supported via \fB--fast-list\fR for efficient directory traversal
.IP \(bu 2
Huawei Drive has a special "applicationData" folder for app-specific data (not accessible via zclone's default configuration)

.SH Error handling
Common errors and their meanings:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB401 Unauthorized\fR: Invalid credentials or expired token
.IP \(bu 2
\fB403 Forbidden\fR: Usually indicates insufficient permissions or API quota exceeded
.IP \(bu 2
\fB404 Not Found\fR: File or directory does not exist
.IP \(bu 2
\fB409 Conflict\fR: Directory already exists
.IP \(bu 2
\fB429 Too Many Requests\fR: API rate limit exceeded, zclone will automatically retry

.SH Performance tuning
For better performance:
.IP \(bu 2
Increase \fB--transfers\fR for concurrent operations (default is 4)
.IP \(bu 2
Adjust \fBchunk_size\fR based on your network speed and file sizes
.IP \(bu 2
Use \fB--fast-list\fR for operations on directories with many files to reduce API calls

.SH Making backups
Huawei Drive is suitable for backups with some considerations:
.IP \(bu 2
Use \fBzclone sync\fR rather than \fBzclone copy\fR to maintain exact directory structure
.IP \(bu 2
Consider using \fB--backup-dir\fR to preserve deleted files
.IP \(bu 2
Verify transfers with \fB--checksum\fR flag for critical data
.IP \(bu 2
Be aware of the 50 GiB file size limit for individual files

.SH Supported features
Huawei Drive supports the following zclone features:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCopy\fR - Server-side copy of files
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMove\fR - Server-side move/rename of files
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirMove\fR - Server-side move of directories
.IP \(bu 2
\fBListR\fR - Recursive listing for \fB--fast-list\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAbout\fR - Storage quota information
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPurge\fR - Delete directory and all contents
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCleanUp\fR - Empty the trash
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUserInfo\fR - Get user account information
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMetadata\fR - Read and write file metadata/properties
.IP \(bu 2
\fBChangeNotify\fR - Poll for remote changes (used by \fBzclone mount\fR and \fBzclone rc vfs/poll-interval\fR)

.SH Integration with other services
Huawei Drive can be used as a backend for various zclone operations:
.IP \(bu 2
Mount as a local filesystem using \fBzclone mount\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Serve over HTTP using \fBzclone serve http\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Serve over FTP using \fBzclone serve ftp\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Serve over WebDAV using \fBzclone serve webdav\fR

.PP
Note that some operations may be slower than local storage due to API limitations and network latency.


.SH HDFS
HDFS
\[la]https://hadoop.apache.org/docs/stable/hadoop\-project\-dist/hadoop\-hdfs/HdfsDesign.html\[ra]
is a distributed file-system, part of the Apache Hadoop
\[la]https://hadoop.apache.org/\[ra]
framework.

.PP
Paths are specified as \fBremote:\fR or \fBremote:path/to/dir\fR\&.

.SH Configuration
