.PP
This remote is called \fBremote\fR and can now be used like this

.PP
See all the top level directories

.EX
zclone lsd remote:
.EE

.PP
List the contents of a directory

.EX
zclone ls remote:directory
.EE

.PP
Sync the remote \fBdirectory\fR to \fB/home/local/directory\fR, deleting any excess files.

.EX
zclone sync --interactive remote:directory /home/local/directory
.EE

.SS Setting up your own HDFS instance for testing
You may start with a manual setup
\[la]https://hadoop.apache.org/docs/stable/hadoop\-project\-dist/hadoop\-common/SingleCluster.html\[ra]
or use the docker image from the tests:

.PP
If you want to build the docker image

.EX
git clone <approved-zclone-repository-or-local-path>
cd zclone/fstest/testserver/images/test-hdfs
docker build --rm -t zclone/test-hdfs .
.EE

.PP
Or you can just use the latest one pushed

.EX
docker run --rm --name "zclone-hdfs" -p 127.0.0.1:9866:9866 -p 127.0.0.1:8020:8020 --hostname "zclone-hdfs" zclone/test-hdfs
.EE

.PP
\fBNB\fP it need few seconds to startup.

.PP
For this docker image the remote needs to be configured like this:

.EX
[remote]
type = hdfs
namenode = 127.0.0.1:8020
username = root
.EE

.PP
You can stop this image with \fBdocker kill zclone-hdfs\fR (\fBNB\fP it does not use
volumes, so all data uploaded will be lost.)

.SS Modification times
Time accurate to 1 second is stored.

.SS Checksum
No checksums are implemented.

.SS Usage information
You can use the \fBzclone about remote:\fR command which will display filesystem
size and current usage.

.SS Restricted filename characters
In addition to the default restricted characters set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]
the following characters are also replaced:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
:	0x3A	：
.TE

.PP
Invalid UTF-8 bytes will also be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra]\&.

.PP
 

