\[la]//docs/#metadata\[ra] docs for more info.

.SH Backend commands
Here are the commands specific to the http backend.

.PP
Run them with:

.EX
zclone backend COMMAND remote:
.EE

.PP
The help below will explain what arguments each command takes.

.PP
See the backend
\[la]//commands/zclone_backend/\[ra] command for more
info on how to pass options and arguments.

.PP
These can be run on a running backend using the rc command
backend/command
\[la]//rc/#backend\-command\[ra]\&.

.SS set
Set command for updating the config parameters.

.EX
zclone backend set remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE

.PP
This set command can be used to update the config parameters
for a running http backend.

.PP
Usage examples:

.EX
zclone backend set remote: [-o opt_name=opt_value] [-o opt_name2=opt_value2]
zclone rc backend/command command=set fs=remote: [-o opt_name=opt_value] [-o opt_name2=opt_value2]
zclone rc backend/command command=set fs=remote: -o url=https://example.com
.EE

.PP
The option keys are named as they are in the config file.

.PP
This rebuilds the connection to the http backend when it is called with
the new parameters. Only new parameters need be passed as the values
will default to those currently in use.

.PP
It doesn't return anything.

.SH Limitations
\fBzclone about\fR is not supported by the HTTP backend. Backends without
this capability cannot determine free space for an zclone mount or
use policy \fBmfs\fR (most free space) as a member of an zclone union
remote.

.PP
See List of backends that do not support zclone about
\[la]///overview/#optional\-features\[ra]
and zclone about
\[la]///commands/zclone_about/\[ra]\&.


.SH ImageKit
This is a backend for the ImageKit.io
\[la]https://imagekit.io/\[ra] storage service.

.PP
ImageKit.io
\[la]https://imagekit.io/\[ra] provides real-time image and video
optimizations, transformations, and CDN delivery. Over 1,000 businesses
and 70,000 developers trust ImageKit with their images and videos on the web.

.PP
To use this backend, you need to create an account
\[la]https://imagekit.io/registration/\[ra]
on ImageKit. Start with a free plan with generous usage limits. Then, as your requirements
grow, upgrade to a plan that best fits your needs. See the pricing details
\[la]https://imagekit.io/plans\[ra]\&.

