.SH iCloud Photos
The iCloud Drive backend also supports accessing iCloud Photos by setting the
\fBservice\fR option to \fBphotos\fR:

.EX
zclone lsd iclouddrive: --iclouddrive-service photos
.EE

.PP
This presents a read-only hierarchy rooted at photo libraries:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLevel 1\fP: Photo libraries — your personal library (\fBPrimarySync\fR) and
any Shared Photo Library (\fBSharedSync-XXXX\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLevel 2+\fP: Albums and folders within a library, nested recursively as in
Apple Photos
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLeaf level\fP: Photos/videos within an album, including Live Photo \fB\&.MOV\fR
companions

.PP
Examples:

.EX
# List libraries
zclone lsd iclouddrive: --iclouddrive-service photos

# List albums in your primary library
zclone lsd iclouddrive:PrimarySync/ --iclouddrive-service photos

# List photos in an album
zclone ls iclouddrive:PrimarySync/All\\ Photos/ --iclouddrive-service photos

# Download a photo
zclone copy iclouddrive:PrimarySync/Favorites/IMG_0001.HEIC /tmp/ --iclouddrive-service photos
.EE

.PP
You can either:
.IP \(bu 2
set \fBservice = photos\fR in \fBzclone config\fR for a dedicated Photos remote
.IP \(bu 2
keep \fBservice = drive\fR and pass \fB--iclouddrive-service photos\fR when needed

.SS Metadata
With \fB--metadata\fR, Photos entries expose these read-only metadata keys:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwidth\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBheight\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBadded-time\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfavorite\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhidden\fR

.PP
These metadata keys are only available when \fBservice = photos\fR\&.

.SS Caching
iCloud Photos caches album listings to disk for fast subsequent access.
On the first run, listing a large album uses parallel \fBstartRank\fR
partitions to fetch pages concurrently. After that, a lightweight change
check (~200ms) determines whether the cache is still valid.

.PP
Cache location: \fB~/.cache/zclone/iclouddrive-photos/<remote>/<zone>/\fR

.PP
To clear the cache: delete that directory or run \fBzclone config reconnect\fR\&.

.SS FUSE mounts
For mounting iCloud Photos via \fBzclone mount\fR, the following flags
are recommended:

.EX
zclone mount remote: /mnt/photos \\
    --iclouddrive-service photos \\
    --vfs-refresh \\
    --dir-cache-time 1h \\
    --vfs-cache-mode full \\
    --attr-timeout 1m \\
    --read-only
.EE

.IP \(bu 2
\fB--vfs-refresh\fR pre-warms directory caches in the background on mount
start so that albums are ready when you browse them
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--dir-cache-time 1h\fR extends the in-memory cache lifetime beyond the
default 5 minutes (change detection is fast, so this is safe)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--vfs-cache-mode full\fR caches downloaded photos and videos to local
disk for fast repeated access
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--attr-timeout 1m\fR reduces kernel attribute lookups (safe because
the backend is read-only)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--read-only\fR prevents confusing write errors

.PP
The first listing of a very large album (e.g. 75,000 items in "All
Photos") can take several minutes due to API pagination limits. This
happens once — subsequent listings use the disk cache.

.SS Limitations
iCloud Photos is read-only. Upload, delete, rename, and move operations
are not supported.

.SH Advanced Data Protection
Advanced Data Protection is supported.

.PP
On iPhone, Settings \fB>\fR Apple Account \fB>\fR iCloud \fB>\fR 'Access iCloud Data on the Web'
must be ON.

.PP
If ADP is enabled on your account, zclone requests PCS cookies after 2FA.
Apple may require approval on a trusted device before those cookies are issued.

.SH Troubleshooting
.SS PCS cookie errors with ADP
If you see \fBMissing PCS cookies from the request\fR or a \fBrequestPCS:\fR error,
the ADP approval flow did not complete successfully.

.PP
Check that 'Access iCloud Data on the Web' is enabled and approve any prompt
on your trusted device.

.PP
Then run \fBzclone reconnect remote:\fR\&.

.PP
If the remote still has stale auth state, clear the \fBcookies\fR and
\fBtrust_token\fR fields in the config, or delete and recreate the remote.

.PP
 

