.SS Metadata
Jottacloud has limited support for metadata, currently an extended set of timestamps.

.PP
Here are the possible system metadata items for the jottacloud backend.

.TS
allbox;
l l l l l 
l l l l l .
\fBName\fP	\fBHelp\fP	\fBType\fP	\fBExample\fP	\fBRead Only\fP
btime	T{
Time of file birth (creation), read from zclone metadata
T}	RFC 3339	T{
2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00
T}	N
content-type	T{
MIME type, also known as media type
T}	string	text/plain	\fBY\fP
mtime	T{
Time of last modification, read from zclone metadata
T}	RFC 3339	T{
2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00
T}	N
utime	T{
Time of last upload, when current revision was created, generated by backend
T}	RFC 3339	T{
2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00
T}	\fBY\fP
.TE

.PP
See the metadata
\[la]//docs/#metadata\[ra] docs for more info.

.SH Limitations
Note that Jottacloud is case insensitive so you can't have a file called
"Hello.doc" and one called "hello.doc".

.PP
There are quite a few characters that can't be in Jottacloud file names.
Zclone will map these names to and from an identical looking unicode
equivalent. For example if a file has a ? in it will be mapped to ？ instead.

.PP
Jottacloud only supports filenames up to 255 characters in length.

.SH Troubleshooting
Jottacloud exhibits some inconsistent behaviours regarding deleted files and
folders which may cause Copy, Move and DirMove operations to previously
deleted paths to fail. Emptying the trash should help in such cases.


.SH Koofr
Paths are specified as \fBremote:path\fR

.PP
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g. \fBremote:directory/subdirectory\fR\&.

