.SH Mail.ru Cloud
Mail.ru Cloud
\[la]https://cloud.mail.ru/\[ra] is a cloud storage provided by a
Russian internet company Mail.Ru Group
\[la]https://mail.ru\[ra]\&. The official
desktop client is Disk-O:
\[la]https://disk\-o.cloud/en\[ra], available on Windows
and Mac OS.

.SH Features highlights
.IP \(bu 2
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g. \fBremote:directory/subdirectory\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Files have a \fBlast modified time\fR property, directories don't
.IP \(bu 2
Deleted files are by default moved to the trash
.IP \(bu 2
Files and directories can be shared via public links
.IP \(bu 2
Partial uploads or streaming are not supported, file size must be known before
upload
.IP \(bu 2
Maximum file size is limited to 2G for a free account, unlimited for paid accounts
.IP \(bu 2
Storage keeps hash for all files and performs transparent deduplication,
the hash algorithm is a modified SHA1
.IP \(bu 2
If a particular file is already present in storage, one can quickly submit file
hash instead of long file upload (this optimization is supported by zclone)

.SH Configuration
Here is an example of making a mailru configuration.

.PP
First create a Mail.ru Cloud account and choose a tariff.

.PP
You will need to log in and create an app password for zclone. Zclone
\fBwill not work\fP with your normal username and password - it will
give an error like \fBoauth2: server response missing access_token\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Click on your user icon in the top right
.IP \(bu 2
Go to Security / "Пароль и безопасность"
.IP \(bu 2
Click password for apps / "Пароли для внешних приложений"
.IP \(bu 2
Add the password - give it a name - eg "zclone"
.IP \(bu 2
Select the permissions level. For some reason just "Full access to Cloud"
(WebDav) doesn't work for Zclone currently. You have to select "Full access
to Mail, Cloud and Calendar" (all protocols).
(thread on forum.zclone.org
\[la]/\[ra])
.IP \(bu 2
Copy the password and use this password below - your normal login password
won't work.

.PP
Now run

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:

.EX
No remotes found, make a new one?
