.SS Process \fBkilled\fR
On accounts with large files or something else, memory usage can significantly
increase when executing list/sync instructions. When running on cloud providers
(like AWS with EC2), check if the instance type has sufficient memory/CPU to
execute the commands. Use the resource monitoring tools to inspect after sending
the commands. Look at this issue
\[la]/\[ra]\&.

.SH Limitations
This backend uses the go-mega go library
\[la]https://github.com/t3rm1n4l/go\-mega\[ra]
which is an opensource
go library implementing the Mega API. There doesn't appear to be any
documentation for the mega protocol beyond the mega C++ SDK
\[la]https://github.com/meganz/sdk\[ra]
source code so there are likely quite a few errors still remaining in this library.

.PP
Mega allows duplicate files which may confuse zclone.


.SH Memory
The memory backend is an in RAM backend. It does not persist its
data - use the local backend for that.

.PP
The memory backend behaves like a bucket-based remote (e.g. like
s3). Because it has no parameters you can just use it with the
\fB:memory:\fR remote name.

.SH Configuration
You can configure it as a remote like this with \fBzclone config\fR too if
you want to:

.EX
No remotes found, make a new one\\?
n) New remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config
n/s/q> n
name> remote
Type of storage to configure.
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value
[snip]
XX / Memory
   \\ "memory"
[snip]
Storage> memory
** See help for memory backend at: //memory/ **

Remote config

Configuration complete.
Options:
- type: memory
Keep this "remote" remote?
y) Yes this is OK (default)
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote
y/e/d> y
.EE

.PP
Because the memory backend isn't persistent it is most useful for
testing or with an zclone server or zclone mount, e.g.

.EX
zclone mount :memory: /mnt/tmp
zclone serve webdav :memory:
zclone serve sftp :memory:
.EE

.SS Modification times and hashes
The memory backend supports MD5 hashes and modification times accurate to 1 nS.

.SS Restricted filename characters
The memory backend replaces the default restricted characters
set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]\&.

.PP
 

.SS Advanced options
Here are the Advanced options specific to memory (In memory object storage system.).

.SS --memory-discard
If set all writes will be discarded and reads will return an error

.PP
If set then when files are uploaded the contents not be saved. The
files will appear to have been uploaded but will give an error on
read. Files will have their MD5 sum calculated on upload which takes
very little CPU time and allows the transfers to be checked.

.PP
This can be useful for testing performance.

.PP
Probably most easily used by using the connection string syntax:

.EX
:memory,discard:bucket
.EE

.PP
