.IP \(bu 2
Type:        string
.IP \(bu 2
Required:    false


.SH Akamai NetStorage
Paths are specified as \fBremote:\fR
You may put subdirectories in too, e.g. \fBremote:/path/to/dir\fR\&.
If you have a CP code you can use that as the folder after the domain such
as <domain>\\/<cpcode>\\/<internal directories within cpcode>.

.PP
For example, this is commonly configured with or without a CP code:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWith a CP code\fP\&. \fB[your-domain-prefix]-nsu.akamaihd.net/123456/subdirectory/\fR
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWithout a CP code\fP\&. \fB[your-domain-prefix]-nsu.akamaihd.net\fR

.PP
See all buckets

.EX
zclone lsd remote:
.EE

.PP
The initial setup for Netstorage involves getting an account and secret.
Use \fBzclone config\fR to walk you through the setup process.

.SH Configuration
Here's an example of how to make a remote called \fBns1\fR\&.
.IP "  1." 5
To begin the interactive configuration process, enter this command:

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.RS
.IP "  1." 5
Type \fBn\fR to create a new remote.
\fBtext
n) New remote
d) Delete remote
q) Quit config
e/n/d/q> n
\fR
.RE
.IP "  2." 5
For this example, enter \fBns1\fR when you reach the name> prompt.

.EX
name> ns1
.EE

.RS
.IP "  1." 5
Enter \fBnetstorage\fR as the type of storage to configure.
\fBtext
Type of storage to configure.
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value
XX / NetStorage
\\ "netstorage"
Storage> netstorage
\fR
.RE
.IP "  3." 5
Select between the HTTP or HTTPS protocol. Most users should choose HTTPS,
which is the default. HTTP is provided primarily for debugging purposes.

.EX
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value
 1 / HTTP protocol
   \\ "http"
 2 / HTTPS protocol
   \\ "https"
protocol> 1
.EE

.RS
.IP "  1." 5
Specify your NetStorage host, CP code, and any necessary content paths using
this format: \fB<domain>/<cpcode>/<content>/\fR
\fBtext
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
host> baseball-nsu.akamaihd.net/123456/content/
\fR
.RE
.IP "  4." 5
Set the netstorage account name

.EX
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
account> username
.EE

.RS
.IP "  1." 5
Set the Netstorage account secret/G2O key which will be used for authentication
purposes. Select the \fBy\fR option to set your own password then enter your secret.
Note: The secret is stored in the \fBzclone.conf\fR file with hex-encoded encryption.
\fBtext
y) Yes type in my own password
g) Generate random password
y/g> y
Enter the password:
password:
Confirm the password:
password:
\fR
.RE
.IP "  5." 5
View the summary and confirm your remote configuration.

.EX
[ns1]
type = netstorage
protocol = http
host = baseball-nsu.akamaihd.net/123456/content/
account = username
secret = *** ENCRYPTED ***
--------------------
y) Yes this is OK (default)
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote
y/e/d> y
.EE

This remote is called \fBns1\fR and can now be used.

.SH Example operations
Get started with zclone and NetStorage with these examples. For additional zclone
commands, visit <//commands/>.

.SS See contents of a directory in your project
.EX
zclone lsd ns1:/974012/testing/
.EE

.SS Sync the contents local with remote
.EX
zclone sync . ns1:/974012/testing/
.EE

.SS Upload local content to remote
.EX
zclone copy notes.txt ns1:/974012/testing/
.EE

.SS Delete content on remote
.EX
zclone delete ns1:/974012/testing/notes.txt
.EE

.SS Move or copy content between CP codes
Your credentials must have access to two CP codes on the same remote.
You can't perform operations between different remotes.

.EX
zclone move ns1:/974012/testing/notes.txt ns1:/974450/testing2/
.EE

.SH Features
.SS Symlink Support
The Netstorage backend changes the zclone \fB--links, -l\fR behavior. When uploading,
instead of creating the .zclonelink file, use the "symlink" API in order to create
the corresponding symlink on the remote. The .zclonelink file will not be created,
the upload will be intercepted and only the symlink file that matches the source
file name with no suffix will be created on the remote.

.PP
This will effectively allow commands like copy/copyto, move/moveto and sync to
upload from local to remote and download from remote to local directories with
symlinks. Due to internal zclone limitations, it is not possible to upload an
individual symlink file to any remote backend. You can always use the "backend
symlink" command to create a symlink on the NetStorage server, refer to "symlink"
section below.

.PP
Individual symlink files on the remote can be used with the commands like "cat"
to print the destination name, or "delete" to delete symlink, or copy, copy/to
and move/moveto to download from the remote to local. Note: individual symlink
files on the remote should be specified including the suffix .zclonelink.

.PP
\fBNote\fP: No file with the suffix .zclonelink should ever exist on the server
since it is not possible to actually upload/create a file with .zclonelink suffix
with zclone, it can only exist if it is manually created through a non-zclone
method on the remote.

.SS Implicit vs. Explicit Directories
With NetStorage, directories can exist in one of two forms:
.IP "  1." 5
\fBExplicit Directory\fP\&. This is an actual, physical directory that you have
created in a storage group.
.IP "  2." 5
\fBImplicit Directory\fP\&. This refers to a directory within a path that has
not been physically created. For example, during upload of a file, nonexistent
subdirectories can be specified in the target path. NetStorage creates these
as "implicit." While the directories aren't physically created, they exist
implicitly and the noted path is connected with the uploaded file.

.PP
Zclone will intercept all file uploads and mkdir commands for the NetStorage
remote and will explicitly issue the mkdir command for each directory in the
uploading path. This will help with the interoperability with the other Akamai
services such as SFTP and the Content Management Shell (CMShell). Zclone will
not guarantee correctness of operations with implicit directories which might
have been created as a result of using an upload API directly.

.SS \fB--fast-list\fR / ListR support
NetStorage remote supports the ListR feature by using the "list" NetStorage API
action to return a lexicographical list of all objects within the specified CP
code, recursing into subdirectories as they're encountered.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBZclone will use the ListR method for some commands by default\fP\&. Commands
such as \fBlsf -R\fR will use ListR by default. To disable this, include the
\fB--disable listR\fR option to use the non-recursive method of listing objects.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBZclone will not use the ListR method for some commands\fP\&. Commands such as
\fBsync\fR don't use ListR by default. To force using the ListR method, include the
\fB--fast-list\fR option.

.PP
There are pros and cons of using the ListR method, refer to zclone documentation
\[la]///docs/#fast\-list\[ra]\&.
In general, the sync command over an existing deep tree on the remote will
run faster with the "--fast-list" flag but with extra memory usage as a side effect.
It might also result in higher CPU utilization but the whole task can be completed
faster.

.PP
\fBNote\fP: There is a known limitation that "lsf -R" will display number of files
in the directory and directory size as -1 when ListR method is used. The workaround
is to pass "--disable listR" flag if these numbers are important in the output.

.SS Purge
NetStorage remote supports the purge feature by using the "quick-delete"
NetStorage API action. The quick-delete action is disabled by default for security
reasons and can be enabled for the account through the Akamai portal. Zclone
will first try to use quick-delete action for the purge command and if this
functionality is disabled then will fall back to a standard delete method.

.PP
\fBNote\fP: Read the NetStorage Usage API
\[la]https://learn.akamai.com/en\-us/webhelp/netstorage/netstorage\-http\-api\-developer\-guide/GUID\-15836617\-9F50\-405A\-833C\-EA2556756A30.html\[ra]
for considerations when using "quick-delete". In general, using quick-delete
method will not delete the tree immediately and objects targeted for
quick-delete may still be accessible.

.PP
 

