.PP
See the remote setup docs
\[la]//remote_setup/\[ra] for how to set it up on a
machine without an internet-connected web browser available.

.PP
Note that zclone runs a webserver on your local machine to collect the
token as returned from Microsoft. This only runs from the moment it
opens your browser to the moment you get back the verification
code.  This is on \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:53682/\fR and this it may require
you to unblock it temporarily if you are running a host firewall.

.PP
Once configured you can then use \fBzclone\fR like this (replace \fBremote\fR with the
name you gave your remote):

.PP
List directories in top level of your OneDrive

.EX
zclone lsd remote:
.EE

.PP
List all the files in your OneDrive

.EX
zclone ls remote:
.EE

.PP
To copy a local directory to an OneDrive directory called backup

.EX
zclone copy /home/source remote:backup
.EE

.SS Getting your own Client ID and Key
zclone uses a default Client ID when talking to OneDrive, unless a custom
\fBclient_id\fR is specified in the config. The default Client ID and Key are
shared by all zclone users when performing requests.

.PP
You may choose to create and use your own Client ID, in case the default one
does not work well for you. For example, you might see throttling.

.SS Creating Client ID for OneDrive Personal
To create your own Client ID, please follow these steps:
.IP "  1." 5
Open 
\[la]https://portal.azure.com/?quickstart=true#view/Microsoft_AAD_IAM/ActiveDirectoryMenuBlade/~/Overview\[ra]
and then under the \fBAdd\fR menu click \fBApp registration\fR\&.
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
If you have not created an Azure account, you will be prompted to. This is free,
but you need to provide a phone number, address, and credit card for identity
verification.
.RE
.IP "  2." 5
Enter a name for your app, choose account type \fBAccounts in any organizational
directory (Any Azure AD directory - Multitenant) and personal Microsoft accounts
(e.g. Skype, Xbox)\fR,
select \fBWeb\fR in \fBRedirect URI\fR, then type (do not copy and paste)
\fBhttp://localhost:53682/\fR and click Register. Copy and keep the
\fBApplication (client) ID\fR under the app name for later use.
.IP "  3." 5
Under \fBmanage\fR select \fBCertificates & secrets\fR, click \fBNew client secret\fR\&.
Enter a description (can be anything) and set \fBExpires\fR to 24 months.
Copy and keep that secret \fIValue\fP for later use (you \fIwon't\fP be able to see
this value afterwards).
.IP "  4." 5
Under \fBmanage\fR select \fBAPI permissions\fR, click \fBAdd a permission\fR and select
\fBMicrosoft Graph\fR then select \fBdelegated permissions\fR\&.
.IP "  5." 5
Search and select the following permissions: \fBFiles.Read\fR, \fBFiles.ReadWrite\fR,
\fBFiles.Read.All\fR, \fBFiles.ReadWrite.All\fR, \fBoffline_access\fR, \fBUser.Read\fR and
\fBSites.Read.All\fR (if custom access scopes are configured, select the
permissions accordingly). Once selected click \fBAdd permissions\fR at the bottom.

.PP
Now the application is complete. Run \fBzclone config\fR to create or edit a OneDrive
remote. Supply the app ID and password as Client ID and Secret, respectively.
zclone will walk you through the remaining steps.

.PP
The access_scopes option allows you to configure the permissions requested by zclone.
See Microsoft Docs
\[la]https://docs.microsoft.com/en\-us/graph/permissions\-reference#files\-permissions\[ra]
for more information about the different scopes.

.PP
The \fBSites.Read.All\fR permission is required if you need to
search SharePoint sites when configuring the remote
\[la]/\[ra]\&.
However, if that permission is not assigned, you need to exclude \fBSites.Read.All\fR
from your access scopes or set \fBdisable_site_permission\fR option to true in the
advanced options.

.SS Creating Client ID for OneDrive Business
The steps for OneDrive Personal may or may not work for OneDrive Business,
depending on the security settings of the organization.
A common error is that the publisher of the App is not verified.

.PP
You may try to verify you account
\[la]https://docs.microsoft.com/en\-us/azure/active\-directory/develop/publisher\-verification\-overview\[ra],
or try to limit the App to your organization only, as shown below.
.IP "  1." 5
Make sure to create the App with your business account.
.IP "  2." 5
Follow the steps above to create an App. However, we need a different account
type here: \fBAccounts in this organizational directory only (*** - Single tenant)\fR\&.
Note that you can also change the account type after creating the App.
.IP "  3." 5
Find the tenant ID
\[la]https://docs.microsoft.com/en\-us/azure/active\-directory/fundamentals/active\-directory\-how\-to\-find\-tenant\[ra]
of your organization.
.IP "  4." 5
In the zclone config, set \fBauth_url\fR to \fBhttps://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR_TENANT_ID/oauth2/v2.0/authorize\fR\&.
.IP "  5." 5
In the zclone config, set \fBtoken_url\fR to \fBhttps://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR_TENANT_ID/oauth2/v2.0/token\fR\&.

.PP
Note: If you have a special region, you may need a different host in step 4 and 5.
Here are some hints
\[la]/\[ra]\&.

.SS Using OAuth Client Credential flow
OAuth Client Credential flow will allow zclone to use permissions
directly associated with the Azure AD Enterprise application, rather
that adopting the context of an Azure AD user account.

.PP
This flow can be enabled by following the steps below:
.IP "  1." 5
Create the Enterprise App registration in the Azure AD portal and obtain a
Client ID and Client Secret as described above.
.IP "  2." 5
Ensure that the application has the appropriate permissions and they are
assigned as \fIApplication Permissions\fP
.IP "  3." 5
Configure the remote, ensuring that \fIClient ID\fP and \fIClient Secret\fP are
entered correctly.
.IP "  4." 5
In the \fIAdvanced Config\fP section, enter \fBtrue\fR for \fBclient_credentials\fR and
in the \fBtenant\fR section enter the tenant ID.

.PP
When it comes to choosing the type of the connection work with the
client credentials flow. In particular the "onedrive" option does not
work. You can use the "sharepoint" option or if that does not find the
correct drive ID type it in manually with the "driveid" option.

.PP
To back up any user's data using this flow, grant your Azure AD
application the necessary Microsoft Graph \fIApplication permissions\fP
(such as \fBFiles.Read.All\fR, \fBSites.Read.All\fR and/or \fBSites.Selected\fR).
With these permissions, zclone can access drives across the tenant,
but it needs to know \fIwhich user or drive\fP you want. Supply a specific
\fBdrive_id\fR corresponding to that user's OneDrive, or a SharePoint site
ID for SharePoint libraries. You can obtain a user's drive ID using
Microsoft Graph (e.g. \fB/users/{userUPN}/drive\fR) and then configure it
in zclone. Once the correct drive ID is provided, zclone will back up
that user's data using the app-only token without requiring their
credentials.

.PP
\fBNOTE\fP Assigning permissions directly to the application means that
anyone with the \fIClient ID\fP and \fIClient Secret\fP can access your
OneDrive files. Take care to safeguard these credentials.

.SS Non-admin access to Business OneDrive
If you do not have admin access to your organization's OneDrive for
Business, you can still connect by manually providing the SharePoint
tenant URL and drive ID. This works by overriding the base API URL
from the standard Microsoft Graph endpoint to the SharePoint v2.0
endpoint.

.SS Steps to manually obtain credentials
.IP "  1." 5
Open your browser and navigate to \fBhttps://[your-tenant].sharepoint.com/\fR
.IP "  2." 5
Open Developer Tools (press F12) and go to the \fBNetwork\fP tab.
.IP "  3." 5
Search for \fBdriveAccessToken\fR in the network requests.
.IP "  4." 5
Extract the following information from the response:
\fBjson
".driveUrl": "{tenant_url}/v2.0/drives/{drive_id}",
".driveAccessToken": "access_token={access_token}"
\fR
#### Zclone configuration
Use the extracted values to configure your remote:
\fBini
type = onedrive
token = {"access_token":"{access_token}","token_type":"Bearer","refresh_token":"","expiry":"2045-12-31T23:59:59Z"}
drive_id = {drive_id}
tenant_url = {tenant_url}
drive_type = business
\fR

.PP
Since the exact expiry time cannot be determined from web traffic,
set the expiry to a future date. Note that the token will eventually
expire and you will need to repeat the process to obtain a new one.

.SS Modification times and hashes
OneDrive allows modification times to be set on objects accurate to 1
second.  These will be used to detect whether objects need syncing or
not.

.PP
OneDrive Personal, OneDrive for Business and Sharepoint Server support
QuickXorHash
\[la]https://docs.microsoft.com/en\-us/onedrive/developer/code\-snippets/quickxorhash\[ra]\&.

.PP
Before zclone 1.62 the default hash for Onedrive Personal was \fBSHA1\fR\&.
For zclone 1.62 and above the default for all Onedrive backends is
\fBQuickXorHash\fR\&.

.PP
Starting from July 2023 \fBSHA1\fR support is being phased out in Onedrive
Personal in favour of \fBQuickXorHash\fR\&. If necessary the
\fB--onedrive-hash-type\fR flag (or \fBhash_type\fR config option) can be used
to select \fBSHA1\fR during the transition period if this is important
your workflow.

.PP
For all types of OneDrive you can use the \fB--checksum\fR flag.

.SS --fast-list
This remote supports \fB--fast-list\fR which allows you to use fewer
transactions in exchange for more memory. See the zclone
docs
\[la]//docs/#fast\-list\[ra] for more details.

.PP
This must be enabled with the \fB--onedrive-delta\fR flag (or \fBdelta =
true\fR in the config file) as it can cause performance degradation.

.PP
It does this by using the delta listing facilities of OneDrive which
returns all the files in the remote very efficiently. This is much
more efficient than listing directories recursively and is Microsoft's
recommended way of reading all the file information from a drive.

.PP
This can be useful with \fBzclone mount\fR and zclone rc vfs/refresh
recursive=true
\[la]//rc/#vfs\-refresh\[ra]) to very quickly fill the mount with
information about all the files.

.PP
The API used for the recursive listing (\fBListR\fR) only supports listing
from the root of the drive. This will become increasingly inefficient
the further away you get from the root as zclone will have to discard
files outside of the directory you are using.

.PP
Some commands (like \fBzclone lsf -R\fR) will use \fBListR\fR by default - you
can turn this off with \fB--disable ListR\fR if you need to.

.SS Restricted filename characters
In addition to the default restricted characters set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]
the following characters are also replaced:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
"	0x22	＂
*	0x2A	＊
:	0x3A	：
<	0x3C	＜
>	0x3E	＞
?	0x3F	？
	0x5C	＼
|	0x7C	｜
.TE

.PP
File names can also not end with the following characters.
These only get replaced if they are the last character in the name:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
SP	0x20	␠
\&.	0x2E	．
.TE

.PP
File names can also not begin with the following characters.
These only get replaced if they are the first character in the name:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
SP	0x20	␠
~	0x7E	～
.TE

.PP
Invalid UTF-8 bytes will also be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra],
as they can't be used in JSON strings.

.SS Deleting files
Any files you delete with zclone will end up in the trash.  Microsoft
doesn't provide an API to permanently delete files, nor to empty the
trash, so you will have to do that with one of Microsoft's apps or via
the OneDrive website.

.PP
 

