.SH Storage usage
The storage usage in Quatrix is restricted to the account during the purchase.
You can restrict any user with a smaller storage limit. The account limit is
applied if the user has no custom storage limit. Once you've reached the limit,
the upload of files will fail. This can be fixed by freeing up the space or
increasing the quota.

.SH Server-side operations
Quatrix supports server-side operations (copy and move). In case of conflict,
files are overwritten during server-side operation.


.SH Sia
Sia (sia.tech
\[la]https://sia.tech/\[ra]) is a decentralized cloud storage platform
based on the blockchain
\[la]https://wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockchain\[ra] technology.
With zclone you can use it like any other remote filesystem or mount Sia folders
locally. The technology behind it involves a number of new concepts such as
Siacoins and Wallet, Blockchain and Consensus, Renting and Hosting, and so on.
If you are new to it, you'd better first familiarize yourself using their
excellent support documentation
\[la]https://support.sia.tech/\[ra]\&.

.SH Introduction
Before you can use zclone with Sia, you will need to have a running copy of
\fBSia-UI\fR or \fBsiad\fR (the Sia daemon) locally on your computer or on local
network (e.g. a NAS). Please follow the Get started
\[la]https://sia.tech/get\-started\[ra]
guide and install one.

.PP
zclone interacts with Sia network by talking to the Sia daemon via HTTP API
\[la]https://docs.sia.tech/\[ra]
which is usually available on port \fI9980\fP\&. By default you will run the daemon
locally on the same computer so it's safe to leave the API password blank
(the API URL will be \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:9980\fR making external access impossible).

.PP
However, if you want to access Sia daemon running on another node, for example
due to memory constraints or because you want to share single daemon between
several zclone and Sia-UI instances, you'll need to make a few more provisions:
.IP \(bu 2
Ensure you have \fISia daemon\fP installed directly or in
a docker container
\[la]https://github.com/SiaFoundation/siad/pkgs/container/siad\[ra]
because Sia-UI does not support this mode natively.
.IP \(bu 2
Run it on externally accessible port, for example provide \fB--api-addr :9980\fR
and \fB--disable-api-security\fR arguments on the daemon command line.
.IP \(bu 2
Enforce API password for the \fBsiad\fR daemon via environment variable
\fBSIA_API_PASSWORD\fR or text file named \fBapipassword\fR in the daemon directory.
.IP \(bu 2
Set zclone backend option \fBapi_password\fR taking it from above locations.

.PP
Notes:
.IP "  1." 5
If your wallet is locked, zclone cannot unlock it automatically.
You should either unlock it in advance by using Sia-UI or via command line
\fBsiac wallet unlock\fR\&.
Alternatively you can make \fBsiad\fR unlock your wallet automatically upon
startup by running it with environment variable \fBSIA_WALLET_PASSWORD\fR\&.
.IP "  2." 5
If \fBsiad\fR cannot find the \fBSIA_API_PASSWORD\fR variable or the \fBapipassword\fR file
in the \fBSIA_DIR\fR directory, it will generate a random password and store in the
text file named \fBapipassword\fR under \fBYOUR_HOME/.sia/\fR directory on Unix
or \fBC:\\Users\\YOUR_HOME\\AppData\\Local\\Sia\\apipassword\fR on Windows.
Remember this when you configure password in zclone.
.IP "  3." 5
The only way to use \fBsiad\fR without API password is to run it \fBon localhost\fP
with command line argument \fB--authorize-api=false\fR, but this is insecure and
\fBstrongly discouraged\fP\&.

