.SH Backend commands
Here are the commands specific to the pikpak backend.

.PP
Run them with:

.EX
zclone backend COMMAND remote:
.EE

.PP
The help below will explain what arguments each command takes.

.PP
See the backend
\[la]//commands/zclone_backend/\[ra] command for more
info on how to pass options and arguments.

.PP
These can be run on a running backend using the rc command
backend/command
\[la]//rc/#backend\-command\[ra]\&.

.SS addurl
Add offline download task for url.

.EX
zclone backend addurl remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE

.PP
This command adds offline download task for url.

.PP
Usage examples:

.EX
zclone backend addurl pikpak:dirpath url
zclone backend addurl pikpak:dirpath url -o name=custom_filename.zip
.EE

.PP
Downloads will be stored in 'dirpath'. If 'dirpath' is invalid,
download will fallback to default 'My Pack' folder.

.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 2
"name": Custom filename for the downloaded file.

.SS decompress
Request decompress of a file/files in a folder.

.EX
zclone backend decompress remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE

.PP
This command requests decompress of file/files in a folder.

.PP
Usage examples:

.EX
zclone backend decompress pikpak:dirpath {filename} -o password=password
zclone backend decompress pikpak:dirpath {filename} -o delete-src-file
.EE

.PP
An optional argument 'filename' can be specified for a file located in
\&'pikpak:dirpath'. You may want to pass '-o password=password' for a
password-protected files. Also, pass '-o delete-src-file' to delete
source files after decompression finished.

.PP
Result:

.EX
{
    "Decompressed": 17,
    "SourceDeleted": 0,
    "Errors": 0
}
.EE

.SH Limitations
.SS Hashes may be empty
PikPak supports MD5 hash, but sometimes given empty especially for user-uploaded files.

.SS Deleted files still visible with trashed-only
Deleted files will still be visible with \fB--pikpak-trashed-only\fR even after the
trash emptied. This goes away after few days.


.SH Pixeldrain
This is the backend for Pixeldrain's premium filesystem feature. This is not the
same as pixeldrain's free file sharing product. The filesystem requires either a
Pro subscription or the Prepaid plan. More information on
subscriptions
\[la]https://pixeldrain.com/#pro\[ra]\&.

.PP
An overview of the filesystem's features and limitations is available in the
filesystem guide
\[la]https://pixeldrain.com/filesystem\[ra] on pixeldrain.

.SH Usage with account
To use the personal filesystem you will need a pixeldrain
account
\[la]https://pixeldrain.com/register\[ra] and either the Prepaid plan or one of
the Patreon-based subscriptions. After registering and subscribing, your
personal filesystem will be available at this link: 
\[la]https://pixeldrain.com/d/me\[ra]\&.

.PP
Go to the API keys page
\[la]https://pixeldrain.com/user/api_keys\[ra] on your account
and generate a new API key for zclone. Then run \fBzclone config\fR and use the API
key to create a new backend.

.PP
Example:

.EX
No remotes found, make a new one\\?
