.SS --fast-list
Seafile version 7+ supports \fB--fast-list\fR which allows you to use fewer
transactions in exchange for more memory. See the zclone
docs
\[la]//docs/#fast\-list\[ra] for more details.
Please note this is not supported on seafile server version 6.x

.SS Restricted filename characters
In addition to the default restricted characters set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]
the following characters are also replaced:

.TS
allbox;
l l l 
l l l .
\fBCharacter\fP	\fBValue\fP	\fBReplacement\fP
/	0x2F	／
"	0x22	＂
	0x5C	＼
.TE

.PP
Invalid UTF-8 bytes will also be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra],
as they can't be used in JSON strings.

.SS Seafile and zclone link
Zclone supports generating share links for non-encrypted libraries only.
They can either be for a file or a directory:

.EX
$ zclone link seafile:seafile-tutorial.doc
http://my.seafile.server/f/fdcd8a2f93f84b8b90f4/

.EE

.PP
or if run on a directory you will get:

.EX
$ zclone link seafile:dir
http://my.seafile.server/d/9ea2455f6f55478bbb0d/
.EE

.PP
Please note a share link is unique for each file or directory. If you run a link
command on a file/dir that has already been shared, you will get the exact same link.

.SS Compatibility
It has been actively developed using the seafile docker image
\[la]https://github.com/haiwen/seafile\-docker\[ra]
of these versions:
.IP \(bu 2
6.3.4 community edition
.IP \(bu 2
7.0.5 community edition
.IP \(bu 2
7.1.3 community edition
.IP \(bu 2
9.0.10 community edition

.PP
Versions below 6.0 are not supported.
Versions between 6.0 and 6.3 haven't been tested and might not work properly.

.PP
Each new version of \fBzclone\fR is automatically tested against the latest docker image
\[la]https://hub.docker.com/r/seafileltd/seafile\-mc/\[ra]
of the seafile community server.

.PP
 

