Type:        string
.IP \(bu 2
Required:    false

.SH Limitations
On some SFTP servers (e.g. Synology) the paths are different
for SSH and SFTP so the hashes can't be calculated properly.
You can either use 
\[la]#\-\-sftp\-path\-override\[ra]
or 
\[la]#\-\-sftp\-disable\-hashcheck\[ra]\&.

.PP
The only ssh agent supported under Windows is Putty's pageant.

.PP
The Go SSH library disables the use of the aes128-cbc cipher by
default, due to security concerns. This can be re-enabled on a
per-connection basis by setting the \fBuse_insecure_cipher\fR setting in
the configuration file to \fBtrue\fR\&. Further details on the insecurity of
this cipher can be found
in this paper
\[la]http://www.isg.rhul.ac.uk/~kp/SandPfinal.pdf\[ra]\&.

.PP
SFTP isn't supported under plan9 until this
issue
\[la]https://github.com/pkg/sftp/issues/156\[ra] is fixed.

.PP
Note that since SFTP isn't HTTP based the following flags don't work
with it: \fB--dump headers\fR, \fB--dump bodies\fR, \fB--dump auth\fR\&.

.PP
Note that \fB--timeout\fR and \fB--contimeout\fR are both supported.

.SH rsync.net {#rsync-net}
rsync.net is supported through the SFTP backend.

.PP
See rsync.net's documentation of zclone examples
\[la]https://www.rsync.net/products/zclone.html\[ra]\&.

.SH Hetzner Storage Box {#hetzner-storage-box}
Hetzner Storage Boxes are supported through the SFTP backend on port 23.

.PP
See Hetzner's documentation for details
\[la]https://docs.hetzner.com/robot/storage\-box/access/access\-ssh\-rsync\-borg#zclone\[ra]


.SH Shade
This is a backend for the Shade
\[la]https://shade.inc/\[ra] platform

.SH About Shade
Shade
\[la]https://shade.inc/\[ra] is an AI-powered cloud NAS that makes your cloud files behave like a local drive, optimized for media and creative workflows. It provides fast, secure access with natural-language search, easy sharing, and scalable cloud storage.

.SH Accounts & Pricing
To use this backend, you need to create a free account
\[la]https://app.shade.inc/\[ra] on Shade. You can start with a free account and get 20GB of storage for free.

.SH Usage
Paths are specified as \fBremote:path\fR

.PP
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g. \fBremote:directory/subdirectory\fR\&.

.SH Configuration
Here is an example of making a Shade configuration.

.PP
First, create a create a free account
\[la]https://app.shade.inc/\[ra] account and choose a plan.

.PP
You will need to log in and get the \fBAPI Key\fR and \fBDrive ID\fR for your account from the settings section of your account and created drive respectively.

.PP
Now run

.PP
\fBzclone config\fR

.PP
Follow this interactive process:

.EX
$ zclone config
e) Edit existing remote
n) New remote
d) Delete remote
r) Rename remote
c) Copy remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config
e/n/d/r/c/s/q> n

Enter name for new remote.
name> Shade

Option Storage.
Type of storage to configure.
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value.
[OTHER OPTIONS]
xx / Shade FS
   \\ (shade)
[OTHER OPTIONS]
Storage> xx

Option drive_id.
The ID of your drive, see this in the drive settings. Individual zclone configs must be made per drive.
Enter a value.
drive_id> [YOUR_ID]

Option api_key.
An API key for your account.
Enter a value.
api_key> [YOUR_API_KEY]

Edit advanced config?
y) Yes
n) No (default)
y/n> n

Configuration complete.
Options:
- type: shade
- drive_id: [YOUR_ID]
- api_key: [YOUR_API_KEY]
Keep this "Shade" remote?
y) Yes this is OK (default)
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote
y/e/d> y
.EE

.SS Modification times and hashes
Shade does not support hashes and writing mod times.

.SS Transfers
Shade uses multipart uploads by default. This means that files will be chunked and sent up to Shade concurrently. In order to configure how many simultaneous uploads you want to use, upload the 'concurrency' option in the advanced config section. Note that this uses more memory and initiates more http requests.

.SS Deleting files
Please note that when deleting files in Shade via zclone it will delete the file instantly, instead of sending it to the trash. This means that it will not be recoverable.

.PP
 

