.SH Limitations
Note that Shade is case insensitive so you can't have a file called
"Hello.doc" and one called "hello.doc".

.PP
Shade only supports filenames up to 255 characters in length.

.PP
\fBzclone about\fR is not supported by the Shade backend. Backends without
this capability cannot determine free space for an zclone mount or
use policy \fBmfs\fR (most free space) as a member of an zclone union
remote.

.PP
See List of backends that do not support zclone about
\[la]///overview/#optional\-features\[ra] and zclone about
\[la]//commands/zclone_about/\[ra]

.SH Backend commands
Here are the commands specific to the shade backend.

.PP
Run them with

.EX
zclone backend COMMAND remote:
.EE

.PP
The help below will explain what arguments each command takes.

.PP
See the backend
\[la]//commands/zclone_backend/\[ra] command for more
info on how to pass options and arguments.

.PP
These can be run on a running backend using the rc command
backend/command
\[la]//rc/#backend\-command\[ra]\&.


.SH SMB
SMB is a communication protocol to share files over network
\[la]https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Server_Message_Block\[ra]\&.

.PP
This relies on go-smb2 library
\[la]https://github.com/CloudSoda/go\-smb2/\[ra] for
communication with SMB protocol.

.PP
Paths are specified as \fBremote:sharename\fR (or \fBremote:\fR for the \fBlsd\fR
command.)  You may put subdirectories in too, e.g. \fBremote:item/path/to/dir\fR\&.

.SH Notes
The first path segment must be the name of the share, which you entered when
you started to share on Windows. On smbd, it's the section title in \fBsmb.conf\fR
(usually in \fB/etc/samba/\fR) file.
You can find shares by querying the root if you're unsure (e.g. \fBzclone lsd remote:\fR).

.PP
You can't access the shared printers from zclone, obviously.

.PP
You can't use Anonymous access for logging in. You have to use the \fBguest\fR user
with an empty password instead. The zclone client tries to avoid 8.3 names when
uploading files by encoding trailing spaces and periods. Alternatively,
the local backend
\[la]//local/#paths\-on\-windows\[ra] on Windows can access SMB servers
using UNC paths, by \fB\\\\server\\share\fR\&. This doesn't apply to non-Windows OSes,
such as Linux and macOS.

.SH Configuration
Here is an example of making a SMB configuration.

.PP
First run

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process.

.EX
