.SH Usage
Paths are specified as \fBremote:bucket\fR (or \fBremote:\fR for the \fBlsf\fR
command.)  You may put subdirectories in too, e.g. \fBremote:bucket/path/to/dir\fR\&.

.PP
Once configured you can then use \fBzclone\fR like this.

.SS Create a new bucket
Use the \fBmkdir\fR command to create new bucket, e.g. \fBbucket\fR\&.

.EX
zclone mkdir remote:bucket
.EE

.SS List all buckets
Use the \fBlsf\fR command to list all buckets.

.EX
zclone lsf remote:
.EE

.PP
Note the colon (\fB:\fR) character at the end of the command line.

.SS Delete a bucket
Use the \fBrmdir\fR command to delete an empty bucket.

.EX
zclone rmdir remote:bucket
.EE

.PP
Use the \fBpurge\fR command to delete a non-empty bucket with all its content.

.EX
zclone purge remote:bucket
.EE

.SS Upload objects
Use the \fBcopy\fR command to upload an object.

.EX
zclone copy --progress /home/local/directory/file.ext remote:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.PP
The \fB--progress\fR flag is for displaying progress information.
Remove it if you don't need this information.

.PP
Use a folder in the local path to upload all its objects.

.EX
zclone copy --progress /home/local/directory/ remote:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.PP
Only modified files will be copied.

.SS List objects
Use the \fBls\fR command to list recursively all objects in a bucket.

.EX
zclone ls remote:bucket
.EE

.PP
Add the folder to the remote path to list recursively all objects in this folder.

.EX
$ zclone ls remote:bucket
/path/to/dir/
.EE

.PP
Use the \fBlsf\fR command to list non-recursively all objects in a bucket or a folder.

.EX
zclone lsf remote:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.SS Download objects
Use the \fBcopy\fR command to download an object.

.EX
zclone copy --progress remote:bucket/path/to/dir/file.ext /home/local/directory/
.EE

.PP
The \fB--progress\fR flag is for displaying progress information.
Remove it if you don't need this information.

.PP
Use a folder in the remote path to download all its objects.

.EX
zclone copy --progress remote:bucket/path/to/dir/ /home/local/directory/
.EE

.SS Delete objects
Use the \fBdeletefile\fR command to delete a single object.

.EX
zclone deletefile remote:bucket/path/to/dir/file.ext
.EE

.PP
Use the \fBdelete\fR command to delete all object in a folder.

.EX
zclone delete remote:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.SS Print the total size of objects
Use the \fBsize\fR command to print the total size of objects in a bucket or a folder.

.EX
zclone size remote:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.SS Sync two Locations
Use the \fBsync\fR command to sync the source to the destination,
changing the destination only, deleting any excess files.

.EX
zclone sync --interactive --progress /home/local/directory/ remote:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.PP
The \fB--progress\fR flag is for displaying progress information.
Remove it if you don't need this information.

.PP
Since this can cause data loss, test first with the \fB--dry-run\fR flag
to see exactly what would be copied and deleted.

.PP
The sync can be done also from Storj to the local file system.

.EX
zclone sync --interactive --progress remote:bucket/path/to/dir/ /home/local/directory/
.EE

.PP
Or between two Storj buckets.

.EX
zclone sync --interactive --progress remote-us:bucket/path/to/dir/ remote-europe:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.PP
Or even between another cloud storage and Storj.

.EX
zclone sync --interactive --progress s3:bucket/path/to/dir/ storj:bucket/path/to/dir/
.EE

.SH Limitations
\fBzclone about\fR is not supported by the zclone Storj backend. Backends without
this capability cannot determine free space for an zclone mount or
use policy \fBmfs\fR (most free space) as a member of an zclone union
remote.

.PP
See List of backends that do not support zclone about
\[la]///overview/#optional\-features\[ra]
and zclone about
\[la]///commands/zclone_about/\[ra]\&.

.SH Known issues
If you get errors like \fBtoo many open files\fR this usually happens when the
default \fBulimit\fR for system max open files is exceeded. Native Storj protocol
opens a large number of TCP connections (each of which is counted as an open
file). For a single upload stream you can expect 110 TCP connections to be
opened. For a single download stream you can expect 35. This batch of
connections will be opened for every 64 MiB segment and you should also
expect TCP connections to be reused. If you do many transfers you eventually
open a connection to most storage nodes (thousands of nodes).

.PP
To fix these, please raise your system limits. You can do this issuing a
\fBulimit -n 65536\fR just before you run zclone. To change the limits more
permanently you can add this to your shell startup script,
e.g. \fB$HOME/.bashrc\fR, or change the system-wide configuration,
usually \fB/etc/sysctl.conf\fR and/or \fB/etc/security/limits.conf\fR, but please
refer to your operating system manual.


.SH SugarSync
SugarSync
\[la]https://sugarsync.com\[ra] is a cloud service that enables
active synchronization of files across computers and other devices for
file backup, access, syncing, and sharing.

.SH Configuration
The initial setup for SugarSync involves getting a token from SugarSync which you
can do with zclone. \fBzclone config\fR walks you through it.

.PP
Here is an example of how to make a remote called \fBremote\fR\&.  First run:

.EX
zclone config
.EE

.PP
This will guide you through an interactive setup process:

.EX
No remotes found, make a new one?
n) New remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config
n/s/q> n
name> remote
Type of storage to configure.
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
Choose a number from below, or type in your own value
[snip]
XX / Sugarsync
   \\ "sugarsync"
[snip]
Storage> sugarsync
** See help for sugarsync backend at: //sugarsync/ **

Sugarsync App ID.
Leave blank to use zclone's.
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
app_id> 
Sugarsync Access Key ID.
Leave blank to use zclone's.
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
access_key_id> 
Sugarsync Private Access Key
Leave blank to use zclone's.
Enter a string value. Press Enter for the default ("").
private_access_key> 
Permanently delete files if true
otherwise put them in the deleted files.
Enter a boolean value (true or false). Press Enter for the default ("false").
hard_delete> 
Edit advanced config? (y/n)
y) Yes
n) No (default)
y/n> n
Remote config
Username (email address)> nick@craig-wood.com
Your Sugarsync password is only required during setup and will not be stored.
password:
Configuration complete.
Options:
- type: sugarsync
- refresh_token: https://api.sugarsync.com/app-authorization/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
Keep this "remote" remote?
y) Yes this is OK (default)
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote
y/e/d> y
.EE

.PP
Note that the config asks for your email and password but doesn't
store them, it only uses them to get the initial token.

.PP
Once configured you can then use \fBzclone\fR like this (replace \fBremote\fR with the
name you gave your remote):

.PP
List directories (sync folders) in top level of your SugarSync

.EX
zclone lsd remote:
.EE

.PP
List all the files in your SugarSync folder "Test"

.EX
zclone ls remote:Test
.EE

.PP
To copy a local directory to an SugarSync folder called backup

.EX
zclone copy /home/source remote:backup
.EE

.PP
Paths are specified as \fBremote:path\fR

.PP
Paths may be as deep as required, e.g. \fBremote:directory/subdirectory\fR\&.

.PP
\fBNB\fP you can't create files in the top level folder you have to
create a folder, which zclone will create as a "Sync Folder" with
SugarSync.

.SS Modification times and hashes
SugarSync does not support modification times or hashes, therefore
syncing will default to \fB--size-only\fR checking.  Note that using
\fB--update\fR will work as zclone can read the time files were uploaded.

.SS Restricted filename characters
SugarSync replaces the default restricted characters set
\[la]//overview/#restricted\-characters\[ra]
except for DEL.

.PP
Invalid UTF-8 bytes will also be replaced
\[la]//overview/#invalid\-utf8\[ra],
as they can't be used in XML strings.

.SS Deleting files
Deleted files will be moved to the "Deleted items" folder by default.

.PP
However you can supply the flag \fB--sugarsync-hard-delete\fR or set the
config parameter \fBhard_delete = true\fR if you would like files to be
deleted straight away.

.PP
 

