.SH Limitations
When uploading very large files (bigger than about 5 GiB) you will need
to increase the \fB--timeout\fR parameter.  This is because Yandex pauses
(perhaps to calculate the MD5SUM for the entire file) before returning
confirmation that the file has been uploaded.  The default handling of
timeouts in zclone is to assume a 5 minute pause is an error and close
the connection - you'll see \fBnet/http: timeout awaiting response
headers\fR errors in the logs if this is happening.  Setting the timeout
to twice the max size of file in GiB should be enough, so if you want
to upload a 30 GiB file set a timeout of \fB2 * 30 = 60m\fR, that is
\fB--timeout 60m\fR\&.

.PP
If you get \fB500 Internal Server Error\fR errors just after uploads,
particularly when uploading many files in parallel, then try setting
\fB--yandex-upload-wait 2s\fR\&. Yandex Disk finalizes uploads
asynchronously on its servers and can report an upload as complete
slightly before the file is ready, so accessing the file's metadata
too soon causes these errors. Yandex support recommend waiting
1.5s - 3s after each upload.

.PP
Having a Yandex Mail account is mandatory to use the Yandex.Disk subscription.
Token generation will work without a mail account, but Zclone won't be able to
complete any actions.

.EX
[403 - DiskUnsupportedUserAccountTypeError] User account type is not supported.
.EE


.SH Zoho Workdrive
Zoho WorkDrive
\[la]https://www.zoho.com/workdrive/\[ra] is a cloud storage solution
created by Zoho
\[la]https://zoho.com\[ra]\&.

