.SS Metadata
Depending on which OS is in use the local backend may return only some
of the system metadata. Setting system metadata is supported on all
OSes but setting user metadata is only supported on linux, freebsd,
netbsd, macOS and Solaris. It is \fBnot\fP supported on Windows yet
(see pkg/attrs#47
\[la]https://github.com/pkg/xattr/issues/47\[ra]).

.PP
User metadata is stored as extended attributes (which may not be
supported by all file systems) under the "user.*" prefix.

.PP
Metadata is supported on files and directories.

.PP
When restoring metadata with \fB--metadata\fR zclone applies the
"mode", "uid" and "gid" from the source. These come from the source
remote which may not be trusted, so restoring metadata as root from an
untrusted source can change file ownership and is not recommended. The
setuid, setgid and sticky bits are not restored by default - see the
\fB--local-metadata-restore-special-bits\fR flag.

.PP
Here are the possible system metadata items for the local backend.

.TS
allbox;
l l l l l 
l l l l l .
\fBName\fP	\fBHelp\fP	\fBType\fP	\fBExample\fP	\fBRead Only\fP
atime	Time of last access	RFC 3339	T{
2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00
T}	N
btime	Time of file birth (creation)	RFC 3339	T{
2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00
T}	N
gid	Group ID of owner	decimal number	500	N
mode	File type and mode	octal, unix style	0100664	N
mtime	Time of last modification	RFC 3339	T{
2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00
T}	N
rdev	Device ID (if special file)	hexadecimal	1abc	N
uid	User ID of owner	decimal number	500	N
.TE

.PP
See the metadata
\[la]//docs/#metadata\[ra] docs for more info.

.SH Backend commands
Here are the commands specific to the local backend.

.PP
Run them with:

.EX
zclone backend COMMAND remote:
.EE

.PP
The help below will explain what arguments each command takes.

.PP
See the backend
\[la]//commands/zclone_backend/\[ra] command for more
info on how to pass options and arguments.

.PP
These can be run on a running backend using the rc command
backend/command
\[la]//rc/#backend\-command\[ra]\&.

.SS noop
A null operation for testing backend commands.

.EX
zclone backend noop remote: [options] [<arguments>+]
.EE

.PP
This is a test command which has some options you can try to change the output.

.PP
Options:
.IP \(bu 2
"echo": Echo the input arguments.
.IP \(bu 2
"error": Return an error based on option value.


