.IP \(bu 2
Final listings are now generated from sync results, to avoid needing to re-list (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync is now much more resilient to changes that happen during a bisync run, and far less prone to critical errors / undetected changes (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync is now capable of rolling a file listing back in cases of uncertainty, essentially marking the file as needing to be rechecked next time. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
A few basic terminal colors are now supported, controllable with 
\[la]//docs/#color\-autoneveralways\[ra] (\fBAUTO\fR|\fBNEVER\fR|\fBALWAYS\fR) (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Initial listing snapshots of Path1 and Path2 are now generated concurrently, using the same "march" infrastructure as \fBcheck\fR and \fBsync\fR, for performance improvements and less risk of error. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--resync\fR is now much more efficient (especially for users of \fB--create-empty-src-dirs\fR) (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Google Docs (and other files of unknown size) are now supported (with the same options as in \fBsync\fR) (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Equality checks before a sync conflict rename now fall back to \fBcryptcheck\fR (when possible) or \fB--download\fR, (nielash)
instead of of \fB--size-only\fR, when \fBcheck\fR is not available.
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now fully supports comparing based on any combination of size, modtime, and checksum, lifting the prior restriction on backends without modtime support. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now supports a "Graceful Shutdown" mode to cleanly cancel a run early without requiring \fB--resync\fR\&. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
New \fB--recover\fR flag allows robust recovery in the event of interruptions, without requiring \fB--resync\fR\&. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
A new \fB--max-lock\fR setting allows lock files to automatically renew and expire, for better automatic recovery when a run is interrupted. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now supports auto-resolving sync conflicts and customizing rename behavior with new 
\[la]#conflict\-resolve\[ra], 
\[la]#conflict\-loser\[ra], and 
\[la]#conflict\-suffix\[ra] flags. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
A new 
\[la]#resync\-mode\[ra] flag allows more control over which version of a file gets kept during a \fB--resync\fR\&. (nielash)
.IP \(bu 2
Bisync now supports 
\[la]//docs/#retries\-int\[ra] and 
\[la]/docs/#retries\-sleep\-duration\[ra] (when 
\[la]#resilient\[ra] is set.) (nielash)
