.IP \(bu 2
Major changes
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Files will be copied to a temporary name ending in \fB\&.partial\fR when copying to \fBlocal\fR,\fBftp\fR,\fBsftp\fR then renamed at the end of the transfer. (Janne Hellsten, Nick Craig-Wood)
.IP \(bu 2
This helps with data integrity as we don't delete the existing file until the new one is complete.
.IP \(bu 2
It can be disabled with the --inplace
\[la]//docs/#inplace\[ra] flag.
.IP \(bu 2
This behaviour will also happen if the backend is wrapped, for example \fBsftp\fR wrapped with \fBcrypt\fR\&.
.IP \(bu 2
The s3
\[la]//s3/#s3\-directory\-markers\[ra], azureblob
\[la]/azureblob/#azureblob\-directory\-markers\[ra] and gcs
\[la]/googlecloudstorage/#gcs\-directory\-markers\[ra] backends now support directory markers so empty directories are supported (Jānis Bebrītis, Nick Craig-Wood)
.IP \(bu 2
The --default-time
\[la]//docs/#default\-time\-time\[ra] flag now controls the unknown modification time of files/dirs (Nick Craig-Wood)
.IP \(bu 2
If a file or directory does not have a modification time zclone can read then zclone will display this fixed time instead.
.IP \(bu 2
For the old behaviour use \fB--default-time 0s\fR which will set this time to the time zclone started up.
